#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"It should be no big difference which branch you choose to translate. When "
"Weblate detects the same strings in different\n"
"branches, they will be used for all branches and only have to be translated "
"once. If in doubt, choose the `develop`\n"
"version.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After selecting a project (Documentation or Zammad), you will see different "
"sub-projects and their translation status summarized for all languages. Here "
"you can select one of the \"components\", which is more or less the same as "
"different versions. After selecting one of them, you can see the status of "
"translation for the different languages, as you can see in the following "
"screenshot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:104
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot showing translation status of different languages for the user "
"documentation](/screenshots/weblate-project-overview.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:105
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Translating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After selecting your language you want to translate to, a good starting "
"point is to select \"_Untranslated strings_\" (or the same meaning in your "
"language, depending on what you have set in your profile).  After that, you "
"will finally see the first untranslated string in the upper field and, in "
"theory, you can start to translate. But let's first have a brief look at the "
"user interface of Weblate:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of Weblate translation user "
"interface](/screenshots/weblate-ui.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Breadcrumbs with path** to the current project and language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Translation area** itself. You can find the source string (_\"English "
"(United States)\"_) at the top and the field for your translation "
"(_\"French\"_ in this example)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Glossary**: here you can find common translations in Zammad context. The "
"terms from the glossary are highlighted in the source strings, as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Some useful tabs**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Nearby strings**: shows you the context of the word or string"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Automatic suggestions**: here you can find automatic suggestions from "
"DeepL and suggestions from similar strings, which are already "
"translated. Use the \"_Clone to translation_\" button to insert it in the "
"translation field to apply changes. Use the \"_Accept_\" button to accept "
"the suggested translation and automatically switch to the next string."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Other languages**: here you can get an overview, which languages are "
"translated and you can also see the translated strings (could be useful for "
"languages, which are similar)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:128
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Markup in Strings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:133
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Find some examples for special source strings with applied markup "
"below. Depending on the string, it can be important to keep the markup "
"and/or variables. Also have a look at the [style guide](style-guide) where "
"you can find more information about the syntax and the usage of "
"Markdown/Vitepress features."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:137
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**\\`example-string\\`**\n"
": This is rendered as `example-string`. Depending on the context, it can be "
"translated or not. In any case, use the\n"
"  \\` before and after the string in your translation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:143
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**\\[example\\](/en/path/to/document-or-website\\)**\n"
": This is a link to another page, including the language code. The above "
"\"example\" is the text, which is shown as\n"
"  link text. This part can be translated. For the path, only the `en` may be "
"replaced by the language code you are\n"
"  translating in. Make sure that your language is already present on "
"zammad.org (check it by using the language\n"
"  switcher). Otherwise contact us if you want to have your language "
"activated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/contribute/contribute.md:146
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**\\*\\*example string\\*\\***\n"
": Markup for text (e.g. bold, italics). Alternative: \\_example "
"string\\_. These strings can be translated, but the\n"
"  markup (e.g. `**` or `_`) should be adopted true to meaning.\n"
msgstr ""

