#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:464
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:481
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**How?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the footer bar of the ticket detail view, click on the `Stay on tab ^` "
"button and select your desired option (if the default is still set, "
"otherwise it is labeled as the other options below). You have different "
"options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Stay on tab**: Default option. You have to manually close the tab if you "
"want to remove it from your navigation sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Close tab**: This option closes the tab on each update of the "
"ticket. Might be a good option if you have to deal with many tickets and/or "
"the tickets require many interactions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Close tab on ticket close**: This option only closes the tab when the "
"ticket is updated to the _closed_ state."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your situation differs from ticket to ticket, you can leave **Stay on "
"tab** and use the keyboard shortcut\n"
"[[shift]] [[c]] for changing the ticket state to closed and close the ticket "
"tab.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Text Modules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows text modules "
"feature](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-article-text-template.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have to answer the same question again and again, ask your Zammad "
"admin to create such a text module for you.  They can even include variables "
"like customer name or any other available attribute which get replaced while "
"using it in a ticket. The usage of text modules has benefits like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "You save time while answering tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Answers from you and your colleagues are aligned because you use the same "
"text for answers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the button in the toolbar of the editor or simply write [[:]][[:]] in "
"the editor. Both ways let you search for the desired text module by typing "
"some characters or words of the text or keywords of the text module."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can pick one by clicking on it or by using the up and down arrows "
"followed by [[enter]] on your keyboard. There are some text modules in "
"Zammad which are shipped by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Insert Knowledge Base Article"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows inserting knowledge base "
"article](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-article-insert-kba.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you often have the same or very similar customer requests about an issue "
"of which a knowledge base article exists.  This saves you time because you "
"don't have to switch to the knowledge base and copy/paste content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the button in the toolbar of the editor or simply write [[?]][[?]] in "
"the editor. Both ways let you search for the desired knowledge base article "
"by typing some characters or words."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mention a User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows mentioning a "
"user](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-article-mention.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Ask or request information from your colleagues or mention them in important "
"tickets so they receive notifications for ticket updates and are "
"automatically subscribed to this ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"While writing a ticket article, use the button in the toolbar of the editor "
"or simply type [[@]][[@]]. Both ways let you search for the name of the user "
"you want to mention by typing some characters or the complete name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad displays a list with all possible matches where you can pick one by "
"clicking on it or by using the up and down arrows followed by [[enter]] on "
"your keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Subscribe to a Ticket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:91
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows subscribe "
"feature](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-subscribe.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are interested in the progress of a ticket, you are not the owner, "
"you can subscribe to it. This means you will receive notifications for each "
"update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Activate the \"Subscribe me\" toggle in the ticket side panel to get "
"notifications. If you have been mentioned in a ticket, you are automatically "
"subscribed. Switch the toggle off to stop the notification. The avatars "
"displayed show you who has subscribed to the ticket and is therefore "
"notified of updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:103
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:176
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Macros"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:106
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows macro action "
"menu](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-macro.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have many steps you do over and over again, you should use a macro "
"for that. In such a macro, your admin can pre-define different ticket "
"actions you can apply with just a click. As an example, Zammad ships a "
"\"Close & Tag as Spam\" macro by default. If applied, the user who executes "
"the macro is assigned as owner, a tag **spam** is added and the ticket is "
"closed. It is even possible to run an [AI "
"agent](/en/documentation/use/guides/ai) within a macro on demand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:118
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your admin already created a macro, you can execute it in the ticket "
"detail view by clicking the `^` section of the `Update` button in the right "
"corner of the footer bar (see screenshot above) and select the macro you "
"want to execute."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The macro gets executed immediately and without an additional "
"confirmation!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:124
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can also apply a macro to several ticket at once. Have a loot at [bulk "
"actions](#bulk-actions) how to do that."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:125
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/checklist.md:19
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Checklists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:128
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows a checklist from checklist "
"sidebar](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-checklist.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid "To keep track of tasks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid "To complete tasks in a structured way"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid "To make sure nothing gets forgotten"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid "To make the progress of work more visible"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:140
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Select the **Checklist** tab in the sidebar. If you can't see it, your "
"Zammad admin disabled it. You can only add or edit a checklist, if you have "
"the permission to edit the ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:142
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the checklist sidebar, you can:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Add a checklist: either by creating a new one by clicking on `Add Empty "
"Checklist` or from a template by using `Add From a Template` (if you don't "
"see the template button, there is none)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid "Edit the current checklist:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Rename it by clicking on the title or using the ::a:: menu in the sidebar "
"header."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add checklist items by clicking the ::+:: button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change the text of the checklist items, either by just clicking on it or "
"using the ::a:: menu next to the item."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid "`Reorder` the items by clicking this button and drag & drop the items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid "Delete the complete checklist by using the ::a:: menu in the sidebar header."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:153
#, markdown-text
msgid "There are two features, which are not directly visible:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:156
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can refer to other tickets as a checklist item by using its hook and "
"number in the item text (e.g.  `Ticket#123456`). Such items can't be checked "
"manually, they reflect the state of the referred ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:156
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Fetch the ticket hook and number by going to the desired ticket and either "
"use the copy button ::c:: in the header or\n"
"  use the keyboard shortcut [[.]]. Then you can paste it in the checklist "
"you want to have it included.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:164
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad automatically checks if all checklist items are completed. The check "
"is performed when you set a ticket to \"closed\". If not all items are "
"completed, Zammad will prompt you to either work on the remaining tasks and "
"keep the ticket open or to close it anyway. When referencing other tickets "
"in your checklist, only those which are closed (with a green circle) are "
"considered as completed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:165
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Templates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:171
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Quickly create a ticket with pre-defined attributes like title, text, tags "
"and more saves you time. This requires your admin to create a ticket "
"template."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:176
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the ticket create screen, you can find an `Apply Template ^` button in "
"the footer bar, if a template is available.  Select the template you want to "
"apply and apply changes if desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:177
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/shared-draft.md:1
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/shared-draft.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shared Drafts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:184
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To share a draft with other agents of your group, e.g. to reflect a QA "
"process, instead of \"just\" adding an internal article. In such a draft you "
"can even include changed ticket attributes like priority, state and custom "
"attributes as well as an article with an answer to the customer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:186
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is an optional feature. If you can't see it, your admin has turned it "
"off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:190
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To **save a draft**, use the ::a:: menu in the footer of the ticket details "
"view and select \"Save as draft\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:192
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To **apply an already existing draft**, click on the `Draft Available` "
"button on the left side of the footer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying a draft overwrites your unsaved changes!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:197
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Monitoring Ticket Escalations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:204
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Service Level Agreements (SLAs) ensure timely responses to customer "
"requests. Your administrator sets such goals as responding to all inquiries "
"within eight hours, with optional custom deadlines for specific "
"customers. When such a deadline is passed, the ticket escalates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:211
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad notifies you by default when tickets approach or exceed their "
"deadlines. Configure these notifications in your [profile "
"settings](/en/documentation/use/user-profile#notifications). Zammad also "
"ships a default overview called \"Escalated Tickets\". This overview "
"includes already escalated tickets and tickets which are expected to "
"escalate within the next 10 minutes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:214
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"SLA-relevant tickets display a timestamp in the ticket detail header. Hover "
"over this timestamp to see all escalation stages and deadlines in a "
"popup. It shows all upcoming or reached escalation times based on your SLA "
"configuration:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:216
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows escalation panel by hovering over escalation "
"timestamp](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/escalation-panel.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:217
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The escalation times are calculated based on your business hours. This means "
"when your business hours start at 9:00, a\n"
"ticket is created at 7:00 and you have an 1-hour deadline, it will escalate "
"at 10:00, unless resolved earlier.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:224
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The SLA feature requires a configuration from your admin. In case you don’t "
"see escalation timestamps, either the ticket is not SLA-relevant or the "
"feature is not configured."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:225
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:81
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bulk Actions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:230
#, markdown-text
msgid "If you have to apply the same changes for many ticket, you can save time!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:234
#, markdown-text
msgid "There are 2 places where you can apply bulk actions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:237
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the ticket tab in the [detailed search page](guides/search)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:237
#, markdown-text
msgid "In [Overviews](guides/overviews)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:239
#, markdown-text
msgid "In both places, you can apply bulk actions in different ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:242
#, markdown-text
msgid "By using the side panel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:242
#, markdown-text
msgid "By using the drag & drop overlay"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:248
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To use bulk actions, first select the tickets you want to apply the changes "
"to. Either select the tickets individually by clicking on the checkbox next "
"to them or use the checkbox in the header to select all tickets of the "
"current page. After selecting all tickets of the page, you can even select "
"all tickets which match your current search query or overview condition by "
"clicking on the **Select all XX results** label. The maximum number of "
"selectable tickets for a bulk action is 2000."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:251
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To select a section of consecutive tickets, click on the checkbox of the "
"first ticket, then hold [[shift]] and click on the checkbox of the last "
"ticket. This selects all tickets in between as well. This also works for "
"unselecting tickets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:255
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the number of affected tickets, you might see a small "
"notification after triggering a bulk action, informing you about the "
"progress. The bulk action is performed in the background so you can work on "
"other tickets.  However, until the bulk action is finished, you are not able "
"to start a new bulk action."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:257
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Side panel:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:259
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the bulk action side "
"panel](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/bulk-side-panel-overviews.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:262
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After you selected tickets, click the `Bulk Action` button in the top right "
"corner and change/add attributes by using the fields in the right side "
"panel. The available changes you can apply to tickets are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:269
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:269
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set owner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:269
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set state"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:269
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set priority"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:269
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add a note"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:269
#, markdown-text
msgid "Execute a macro"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:271
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Drag & drop with bulk overlay:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:273
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the bulk action via drag and "
"drop](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/bulk-action-drag-and-drop.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:277
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After you selected tickets, drag them by pressing and holding the mouse "
"button and drop them on the desired action in the bulk action overlay. You "
"can always skip this by dropping the tickets in the middle of the page. The "
"available actions you can apply to tickets are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid "Unassign owner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid "Unassign owner and set group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid "Run macro"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:286
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Start your drag and drop action from one of the already selected tickets in "
"case you selected all relevant ones.  To include another unselected ticket, "
"start dragging from there and so it is also included in the batch "
"processing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:287
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Merge Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:290
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the ticket merge side "
"panel](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-merge.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:296
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have two or more tickets about the same issue, you may want to merge "
"those tickets into one. This might be the case if a customer sends you a new "
"email which can't be assigned to the existing ticket (e.g. the ticket "
"reference is missing because the customer sends you a completely new email "
"instead of answering in the existing thread)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:298
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Merging a ticket migrates all messages and notes of the ticket from where "
"you select the merging into the selected one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:304
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Go to the ticket you want to merge into another one. In the ticket sidebar, "
"use the ::a:: menu and select `Merge`. This opens a side panel in which you "
"can select a ticket by clicking on it or enter a ticket number in search "
"field.  When you selected a target ticket, confirm by using the `Merge` "
"button at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:307
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"As result, the articles are moved into the chosen ticket. The ticket in "
"which you executed the merge still exists with the following changes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:311
#, markdown-text
msgid "The articles have been replaced by a \"merged\" label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:311
#, markdown-text
msgid "The state has changed to \"merged\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:311
#, markdown-text
msgid "The ticket is linked to its \"parent\" ticket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:312
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Split Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:315
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the article action split "
"menu](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-split.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:320
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have a ticket which is about more than one issue, you might want to "
"split it in two or more separate tickets.  For example, this might be the "
"case if a customer has a technical question and wants to place an order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:324
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To split an article off, use the ::a:: menu next to an article and select "
"`Split`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:327
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This results in a ticket create screen with the same attributes set as in "
"the initial ticket. The content of the article is also included. You can "
"change everything to your needs and then click on `Create`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:330
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The just created ticket is linked in the original one as child. The original "
"ticket is linked in the split off ticket as parent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:331
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Link Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:337
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When tickets about related issues arise, they can be linked to each other "
"for easier reference.  [Merged](#merge-tickets) and [split](#split-tickets) "
"tickets are automatically linked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:343
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the ticket sidebar, add a link to another ticket by clicking the ::+:: "
"button in the \"Links\" section. This opens a side panel in which you can "
"select a ticket by clicking on it or enter a ticket number in search "
"field. Additionally, you can choose between different link types:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:347
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Normal:** for related ticket which have no hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:347
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Parent/Child**: for related tickets where one is the main issue and the "
"other is a subtask. This link type is used by default if a tickets gets "
"split or merged."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:348
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Duplicate Detection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:351
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows duplicate ticket warning during ticket "
"creation](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/duplicate-detection.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:357
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Sometimes, it happens that a customer reaches out to you (or colleagues) "
"more than once about a single issue. To avoid creating duplicate tickets, "
"Zammad can warn you when another ticket is already present. This feature has "
"to be activated and configured by your admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:363
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Just create a new ticket and provide some information. Your admin can "
"configure which ticket attributes must match for the warning to show up "
"(e.g. customer and title). In case of many unnecessary warnings or no "
"warning at all, ask your admin to adjust the attributes to compare."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:367
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When a duplicate is detected, a warning in the ticket shows up (see the "
"example in screenshot above). This warning can contain a ticket "
"number. Click on the ticket link to see what it is about. In case it is no "
"duplicate, simply ignore it and continue with the ticket creation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:368
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/time-accounting.md:1
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/time-accounting.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Time Accounting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:375
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"With Zammad's integrated time accounting, you can help to keep track of how "
"much time you spent on tickets. Based on the accounted times in the ticket, "
"it is automatically assigned to customers and organizations. This might be "
"used in your company for billing or to keep track of support budgets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:379
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After updating a ticket, a time accounting dialog will appear. Enter how "
"much time you spent on the ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:381
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the time accounting "
"dialog](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/time-accounting-dialog.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:384
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The feature is **optional**. If you don't see it whenever you update a "
"ticket, your administrator hasn't enabled it yet or the rule for tickets to "
"be taken into consideration doesn't match."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:387
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The accounted time is always recorded and stored without a unit. However, "
"your administrator may decide to show an optional label next to the field to "
"hint you and your colleagues in which unit the time is expected (see "
"screenshot)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:390
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Activity types can be used to distinguish between different activities and "
"for grouping the accounted times. If this optional feature is active, it "
"shows a list of activities from which you can select in the time accounting "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:394
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If a ticket already has accounted time(s), you can see it in the ticket "
"sidebar on the right side in the ticket detail view at the bottom. You can "
"find the calculated sums of each activity type (if configured) as well as "
"the total sum of accounted times for all activity types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:396
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the time accounting "
"overview](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/time-accounting-overview.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:397
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User Detail Panel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:403
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Viewing important customer/user information at a glance without leaving your "
"current view allows you to stay focused on your task."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:409
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You might have seen it already: simply hover your mouse over an avatar icon, "
"no matter if it is in the header, footer, main content or the content "
"sidebar in the ticket detail view. To see more details, click on the user "
"avatar to open the [user detail page](#user-detail-page)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:411
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows an avatar with opened user detail "
"panel](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/user-detail-panel.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:414
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By the way, the crown in the screenshot represents the customer's VIP state, "
"which can be set in the customer detail view and the admin settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:415
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User Detail Page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:418
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows user detail "
"page](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/user-detail-page.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:422
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It allows you to see all relevant user information in one place. Examples "
"what you can find and do there:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:429
#, markdown-text
msgid "See organization membership"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:429
#, markdown-text
msgid "See a graph of recent tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:429
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:449
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add or edit a note"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:429
#, markdown-text
msgid "Edit the customer (via ::a:: menu)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:429
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:449
#, markdown-text
msgid "See a history of changes (via ::a:: menu)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:429
#, markdown-text
msgid "Create a new ticket with this user as customer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:434
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Simply click on a user avatar (e.g. in the header of the ticket detail "
"view). This opens a new tab with the customer detail page. In case you also "
"have admin permissions, you can even create a deletion job for a user from "
"the ::a:: menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:435
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Organization Detail Page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:438
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows organization detail "
"page](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/organization-detail-page.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:442
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It allows you to see all relevant organization information in one "
"place. Examples what you can find and do there:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:449
#, markdown-text
msgid "See the members of the organization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:449
#, markdown-text
msgid "See a graph of the recent tickets of the whole organization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:449
#, markdown-text
msgid "Edit the organization (via ::a:: menu)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:449
#, markdown-text
msgid "Create a new user as a member of this organization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:454
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Simply click on an organization avatar (e.g. in the header of the ticket "
"detail view next to the user avatar). This opens a new tab with the "
"organization detail page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:455
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "External Issues and Assets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:462
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you use i-doit and Zammad for IT support or you deal with Github or "
"Gitlab issues, you can link to these external systems to have all relevant "
"information in one place. Your Zammad admin has to activate and configure "
"these features in Zammad's settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:466
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows Gitlab content sidebar with \"Link Issue\" "
"button](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/gitlab-content-sidebar.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:471
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If activated, simply open a ticket and choose the right content sidebar tab "
"with the respective icon (see Gitlab example in screenshot above). Click the "
"button to link to an issue by entering the URL of it or select the item from "
"a select field (i-doit). Afterwards, you can see the linked item with "
"additional metadata. By clicking on the linked item, you are redirected to "
"it in the respective system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:472
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Highlight Text"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:479
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It allows you to give your colleagues a hint about important aspects of the "
"ticket and to make sure important parts aren't getting overlooked. Be aware "
"that this feature is not about text highlighting for new articles, it is "
"about highlighting text in existing articles for you and other agents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:483
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows highlight menu from ticket detail "
"view](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/text-highlighting.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/advanced-features.md:487
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the highlighting tool with the pencil icon in the upper right corner in "
"the ticket detail view. To highlight text, either select text first and then "
"click the button. As an alternative, you can click the highlighting button "
"first and then select text. You can choose a different color by using the "
"down arrow on the right side of the button. To remove the highlighting, "
"simply choose the rubber icon from the color menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When a customer messages you over a channel which is fetched by Zammad, a "
"ticket is created automatically (unless Zammad recognizes it as a follow-up, "
"then it gets added as an article to an existing ticket). However, there "
"might be cases where you need to create a ticket manually. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "A customer calls you by phone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "You receive a paper letter from a customer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "A customer comes to a physical service desk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "You proactively have to inform a customer by sending out a message."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In situations like these, you need to create a new ticket manually and click "
"the ::+:: button at the bottom of the navigation bar. This shows a ticket "
"create screen where you can add all needed information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows ticket create "
"screen](/screenshots/cypress/usage-basics.cy.js/ticket-create.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Type Selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the ticket create dialog, you can choose from different article types:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "Received call: for issues initiated by a customer over the phone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "Outbound call: for issues initiated by an agent over the phone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "Send email: for issues initiated by an agent over email."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When choosing **Send Email**, the customer receives an email with the title "
"as subject and the text as email content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Title"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is the title of a ticket which is shown in many places in Zammad. For "
"example, this gets displayed in overviews.  It is also used as the subject "
"for email communication. For emails, a ticket identifier is automatically "
"appended (e.g. `Ticket#901234 - I need help!`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Customer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Enter a name or email address of a customer to search for existing "
"accounts. You can even search for organizations and their members. Select an "
"option from the dropdown menu or create a new customer by clicking the `+ "
"Create new Customer` button on the right side of the field. This opens a "
"dialog where you can provide all relevant information of the customer. A "
"ticket can only have one customer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After setting a customer in the ticket create dialog, the customer sidebar "
"automatically opens. You can see additional customer meta information "
"including a hint about the currently opened tickets of the customer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:48
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/object.md:131
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Text"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is the content section where the currently known details of the issue "
"gets written down. For the \"Send Email\" type, this is the content/message "
"of the email. To learn more about the editor and its features, check the "
"[editor documentation](/en/documentation/use/guides/editor)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:54
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Attributes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"As you may know, there are additional ticket attributes such as group, "
"priority and owner that you can set. If you haven't read the [ticket "
"basics](ticket-basics) yet, check it out to learn more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After you provided the relevant information, finally create the ticket with "
"a click on the `Create` button. Read on [how to work with existing "
"tickets](work-with-tickets)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:9
#, markdown-text
msgid "There are different ways to find tickets, depending on your use case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:10
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Via Overviews"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you search for new tickets to work on, your first look should be in the "
"overview section. You can either open it by clicking the `Overviews` button "
"in the navigation bar or use the keyboard shortcut [[o]]. You can see "
"overviews as a kind of ticket lists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, there are some built-in overviews you can use. For example, "
"there is an overview called \"Open Tickets\".  This might be a good starting "
"point. Your Zammad admin may have created additional overviews. These are "
"based on conditions, which are basically rules, to define which ticket "
"appears in which overview."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For a detailed description, head over to the [overview usage "
"guide](/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Via Search"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"However, if you search for a specific ticket which might or might not be "
"visible in the overviews, you can use the search. You can find it in the top "
"left corner in the navigation bar. Either select it via mouse or use the "
"keyboard shortcut by simply pressing [[s]]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After activating the search field, you can find the tickets you recently "
"closed from your taskbar as well as your last search queries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By entering a search term, you immediately see a preview of the search "
"results. If you press [[enter]] or click on `detailed search`, Zammad "
"displays a page with search results. There you can differentiate by object "
"type (e.g.  user), what you are searching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Have a look at the [search guide](/en/documentation/use/guides/search) for "
"more details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:37
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the [notification "
"settings](/en/documentation/use/user-profile#notifications) in your profile, "
"you receive updates for different ticket based events like the creation or "
"the update of a ticket. This ensures that no important change to a ticket "
"gets overlooked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can open them by clicking on the notification counter in the top left "
"corner. If there is a badge with a counter, the counter shows the number of "
"unread notifications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, you get notified when one of your tickets (means you are the "
"owner) got updated. By clicking on the link in the notification, this ticket "
"gets opened in the navigation sidebar as a tab and the ticket detail view is "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Basics"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"New to ticket systems? Then read on about the basics. This helps you to "
"understand the main concepts and to get started with Zammad. If you are "
"already familiar with ticket systems, you can jump directly to the next "
"pages about finding, creating and working with tickets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In Zammad, **tickets** are used to track customer service requests. The "
"first time a customer contacts you about something, Zammad creates a new "
"ticket. Each message sent between you and the customer is added to that "
"ticket until the issue is resolved, the customer is happy and the ticket is "
"finally closed. Such a single message in a ticket is called an "
"**article**. Basically, you can think of a **ticket** as a **conversation** "
"between you and a customer about a single issue."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you're completely new to a ticket system and handled your customer "
"requests with an email client so far, you might think that a ticket system "
"is complicated. But the opposite is true:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"All emails are now collected in Zammad (and requests from other channels "
"might be as well)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You and your colleagues can see who is working on which customer request "
"(\"ticket\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The state of each request as well as the history (who did what?) is "
"transparent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "There is no duplicate work and nothing gets overlooked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can ask your colleagues directly in the ticket for help in difficult "
"cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"With Zammad's intuitive UI, you can focus on what matters: to resolve "
"customer issues and answer customer questions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This means you can work with Zammad in a similar way as with your email "
"client. Except that a ticket has additional attributes. Read on to learn "
"more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In addition to articles, tickets have some additional meta information which "
"are called attributes. Use the **ticket sidebar** to view and change ticket "
"attributes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows ticket "
"sidebar](/screenshots/cypress/usage-basics.cy.js/ticket-sidebar.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To hide the sidebar, click the collapse button with the arrow on the left "
"side of the sidebar. Click on one of the tabs to bring it back. The "
"available options depend on your privileges and the configuration of your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It is even possible to create custom fields for tickets (for groups, users "
"and organizations too). You think such a custom field makes sense? Talk with "
"your Zammad admin, it can be set up easily."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:46
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "State"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The state reflects the current status of a ticket (mainly if a customer "
"request is resolved or not). Think of it as a representation of progress "
"towards completion. By default, there are the following states:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**New**: State for new tickets on which no one has worked on. When updating "
"a ticket for the first time, it automatically switches to open."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Open**: State for tickets which aren't resolved yet and some work needs to "
"be done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Pending Close**: State for tickets which are basically resolved but you "
"don't want to close immediately. This state requires you to enter a date and "
"time at which the ticket automatically switches to closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Pending Reminder**: State for open tickets which you want to get reminded "
"about at a certain date and time. Requires you to enter a date and time at "
"which you want to get notified. For example useful if you had a question to "
"a third party and want to make sure that this issue won't be forgotten."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Merged**: State for a ticket which was merged into another ticket. Check "
"the [linked tickets](/en/documentation/use/advanced-features#link-tickets) "
"to see the related ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad's ticket states are color coded. This helps you to understanding the "
"state of the ticket much faster in general - without having a look into "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows different color-coded "
"states](/screenshots/overviews/states.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Priority"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A ticket's priority is simply a ranking (from 1 to 3) of how urgent or "
"important it is. The three default priorities are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "1 low"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "2 normal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "3 high"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:78
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case these priorities aren't enough, ask your Zammad admin to create "
"additional ones. The default priorities allow you to immediately recognize "
"the importance of your tickets because they are color coded:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows different color-coded "
"priorities](/screenshots/overviews/priorities.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:83
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You might wonder what such a ticket priority is for. Out of the box, it "
"doesn't actually do anything except the highlighting. However, Zammad "
"administrators can set up all sorts of automation and analytics based on the "
"priority."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Be aware that customers can't set a priority for their own "
"tickets. Otherwise, some might set their tickets always to high and hope for "
"an immediate escalation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:87
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/tags.md:1 src/en/reference/rest-api/tags.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Tags are custom labels that can be assigned to tickets to make it easier to "
"find them in the future.  They can be used in conditions like in triggers "
"and in overviews and they can also be assigned automatically by macros, "
"schedulers and triggers. Of course you can search for the text of the tags "
"and you will find the tickets which have the tag assigned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows tag area in ticket side "
"bar](/screenshots/cypress/usage-advanced-features.cy.js/ticket-tags.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the ticket sidebar, you can find a section which is labeled as "
"**Tags**. Add a tag by clicking on the ::+:: button.  Depending on your "
"Zammad's configuration, you can create new tags by simply type and confirm "
"them with [[enter]] or [[tab]]. In any case, you can choose from already "
"available tags. Start typing and you see a list with matching "
"suggestions. To remove it, click the ::X:: button on the right side of the "
"tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:101
#: src/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes.md:1054
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/group.md:1 src/en/reference/rest-api/group.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This ticket attribute is useful for organizations with more than one team. A "
"common way to use groups is to have one for each department of the "
"company. Depending on the permissions, you might not see the ticket after "
"changing the group and saving the changes. In case you can't see the group "
"field, either there is only one group in your Zammad system or you don't "
"have the permission to create a ticket in other groups."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:108
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Owner"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This is the person who is currently responsible for the ticket. In case you "
"need information from another colleague, you can either change the owner to "
"this person or mention the person in an article by typing [[@]][[@]] and "
"selecting the user. In the latter case, the user gets notified and is "
"automatically subscribed to receive notifications on ticket updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:116
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To change the owner to a person which has only access to another group's "
"tickets, you first have to switch the group accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:120
#, markdown-text
msgid "Now that you know the basics, head over to one of the following pages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Find Tickets](/en/documentation/use/basics/find-tickets)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Create tickets](/en/documentation/use/basics/create-tickets)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Work with tickets](/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Work with Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:9
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You found your way into an existing ticket, congratulations! Now let's have "
"a look what you can do and how to do it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Generally, working on existing tickets means keeping up with a customer "
"correspondence in a thread/conversation in the ticket detail view. Any time "
"you open a ticket, a new tab will appear in your navigation bar on the left "
"side. To close a tab (in the sense of remove it from the navigation bar, not "
"setting the ticket state to closed), just click the ::X:: button in the "
"tab. Zammad automatically saves your changes in opened ticket tabs, no "
"matter if you already applied the changes or just edited things and switched "
"to somewhere else. This means it is no problem to create a new ticket while "
"editing an existing one. Simply switch back to the other tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For the most changes (except tags or title renaming, for example), an "
"explicit update of the ticket is needed. So make sure to click the `Update` "
"button on the right side of the footer bar when you are happy with your "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Changing Ticket Attributes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"As you may know, there are additional ticket attributes such as group, "
"priority and owner that you can set. If you haven't read "
"[ticket-basics](/en/documentation/use/basics/ticket-basics) yet, check it "
"out to learn more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a New Article"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"No matter if you create a new article from scratch or respond to a customer "
"article, you can choose from different article types:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Note**: Write a reminder for yourself and other agents, ask a colleague a "
"question by mentioning a user or add new information to the ticket. The "
"default visibility is \"internal\", which means the customer can't see the "
"note."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Call**: Note down a summary of a phone call you had with the customer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Email**: Send an email to anyone about the ticket. The title of the ticket "
"is used for the subject of the email."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To choose another article type, click the **Channel** dropdown and choose a "
"different type. Click on the **Visibility** dropdown to change the article's "
"visibility. Articles with \"internal\" visibility are displayed with a "
"dashed blue border."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows article type and visibility "
"selector](/screenshots/cypress/usage-basics.cy.js/article-type-visibility.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To write and edit text, make use of the powerful editor features. You can "
"use the toolbar or keyboard shortcuts to format text and trigger special "
"functions. Because of the amount of features and their importance, you can "
"find more information on the separate [editor "
"page](/en/documentation/use/guides/editor)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Every new article appears at the end of the conversation, which means below "
"the existing articles. To see detailed information of an article, just click "
"on an existing article which opens additional meta information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You might wonder now how to delete articles. The answer is you can only "
"delete articles that you have created yourself and which are not older than "
"10 minutes. To see the **Delete article** function in the ::a:: menu, "
"articles of a communication type (emails, calls) must be changed to "
"\"internal\" visibility first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add an Article from Scratch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Click on one of the buttons at the bottom of the ticket detail view to add "
"an article. Depending on what you choose, the article create screen gets "
"pre-populated with the type and visibility. When choosing **Add reply**, the "
"article gets sent out to the customer of the ticket. In case of an email "
"based ticket, the email address of the customer is pre-populated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows new article buttons in bottom "
"bar](/screenshots/cypress/usage-basics.cy.js/new-article.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Respond to an Article"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To forward or reply to an article, use one of the response buttons under an "
"article or in the ::a:: menu. The behavior is similar to the behavior of an "
"email client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:72
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Reply**: Allows you to answer the article. The recipient is automatically "
"pre-filled. The reply is sent via the same channel as the original "
"message. This lets you easily send an answer to a customer or third party, "
"if involved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:72
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Reply all**: Same as above but uses all recipient addresses from the "
"original message as recipients for your new article. Only available for "
"email channels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:72
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Forward**: This means you can forward the original message to a third "
"party or anybody else. The original message and attachments are included in "
"your new article."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows article reply "
"actions](/screenshots/cypress/usage-basics.cy.js/article-reply.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:83
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad even allows you to **quote text** from an existing article. This is "
"especially helpful if an answer refers to different parts of the original "
"message or the text is pretty long. This feature is limited to communication "
"type articles like email where the response buttons are available. To quote "
"text, simply select the text you want to quote and use the **Reply** or "
"**Reply all** function. This adds the selected text with a timestamp in your "
"article editor where you can answer it. You can use the quoting even "
"multiple times to quote different parts of the text. Just select another "
"part of the text, click on the same response action as before and it gets "
"added as another quote to your editor.  You can split quotations by using "
"[[enter]] or [[shift]] + [[enter]] in the editor and disable quote format "
"for your text."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:84
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rename a Ticket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:89
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To rename a ticket, simply click on the title in the header bar and start "
"typing. This title is used as subject in email communication and shows up in "
"several places like overviews. Confirm with [[enter]] or click the button on "
"the right side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:90
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy Ticket Number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To copy the ticket number including a link to the ticket (e.g. to paste it "
"in a third party chat app), use the ::c:: icon next to the ticket title. It "
"copies the complete ticket number with the ticket identifier to your "
"clipboard, e.g.  `Ticket#50071`. If pasting the content to a target which "
"can handle HTML, a link to the ticket is included. If you just want to paste "
"the ticket number, use plain pasting via [[ctrl]] [[shift]] [[v]] instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:99
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you scrolled own in the ticket, hover over the collapsed header bar where "
"you can find the button on the top left side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows ticket header with highlighted ticket number copy "
"button](/screenshots/cypress/usage-basics.cy.js/copy-ticket-number-button.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:105
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"But wait, there is even a keyboard shortcut for that! Simply press [[.]] in "
"the ticket detail view and the ticket number is copied to your clipboard. To "
"include the ticket title as well, press [[.]] twice.  Example: "
"`Ticket#31004: Onboarding new colleague`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:106
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Simultaneous Ticket Processing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It can happen that two or more agents open a ticket at the same time. To "
"prevent edit conflicts and customers receiving contradictory answers, Zammad "
"shows you who is viewing or editing the ticket currently. You can find this "
"information in the bottom bar where avatars of all agents are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows other agents viewing/editing the "
"ticket](/screenshots/advanced-features/simultaneous-work-detection.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:116
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Make sure to communicate with your colleagues to prevent these problems "
"before they arise. Depending on the additional icon and if the avatar icon "
"is faded, it means:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:120
#, markdown-text
msgid "Avatar: Another agent is viewing the ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:120
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Faded avatar: Another agent opened the ticket but is currently not actively "
"viewing it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:120
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Avatar with pencil icon: Another agent is currently actively working on this "
"ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There are even more icons which represent additional states of the other "
"agents (e.g. viewing ticket by mobile UI or is out-of-office). Just hover "
"with the mouse if you are unsure what it means."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:124
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Actions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:127
#, markdown-text
msgid "Additional actions are available in the ::a:: menu in the ticket sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:131
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"History\n"
": See a comprehensive list of updates to the ticket, performed by any user, "
"since its creation. Useful to check who did\n"
"  what and when.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:135
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Merge\n"
": Migrate all messages/notes to another ticket. Useful if you have more than "
"one ticket about a single customer issue.\n"
"  See [Merge Tickets](/en/documentation/use/advanced-features#merge-tickets) "
"for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:138
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change Customer : Reassign the ticket to another customer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/work-with-tickets.md:143
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You now know the basics and how to work with tickets in general. However, "
"there are many more features in Zammad which can be very useful in your "
"daily work. Read on in [Advanced "
"Features](/en/documentation/use/advanced-features) to learn more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad UI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The user interface (UI) of Zammad is designed to provide an intuitive "
"experience for users. It is built around the concept of simplicity, clarity, "
"and accessibility and is based on common software design principles which "
"should make the UI pretty self explanatory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There are basic modular components for different features to keep the UI "
"consistent. These components are described in the sections below. Depending "
"on the currently opened screen, there are interactive components, such as "
"tooltips and a contextual help. Use them wherever needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the ticket detail "
"view](/screenshots/cypress/zammad-ui.cy.js/zammad-ui-full.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Main UI Elements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The screenshot above shows a ticket detail view in Zammad. Read on for a "
"description of the different main elements of Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Navigation Sidebar\n"
": This is the left sidebar which includes the search, notifications, "
"overviews, ticket tabs, your avatar and the ticket\n"
"  create button.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Navigation Tab\n"
": Each item of the navigation sidebar is called navigation tab. Depending on "
"the content, it can be a ticket tab (with\n"
"  the ticket detail view) or the overview tab which opens the list of "
"available overviews.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ticket Detail View\n"
": This is where you handle your customer requests. It is located in the "
"middle of the screen if a ticket tab is\n"
"  selected in the navigation sidebar.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:38
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sidebar\n"
": This is the right sidebar in the ticket detail view. It contains sidebar "
"tabs like customers and checklists and\n"
"  displays the currently selected tab.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sidebar Tabs\n"
": On the right side of the sidebar, you can find small icons to switch "
"between the different tabs. The availability of\n"
"  these tabs depends on your system configuration, your permissions and the "
"ticket attributes (e.g. if the ticket\n"
"  customer has an assigned organization).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The navigation sidebar is your central place to access all main parts of "
"Zammad. You might not see all of them because some depend on the "
"configuration of your Zammad. The navigation sidebar is always visible. That "
"means if you don’t know where you are, you can always go back to the "
"dashboard, your overviews or an opened ticket, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:54
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Search and Notfication Area\n"
": Includes the search where you can search for users, organizations, tickets "
"and basically every in Zammad available\n"
"  information. Next to the search you can find the Zammad logo. In case "
"there is a notification, it shows you a badge\n"
"  with a count about how many notifications you got.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Navigation : Allows you to switch to different Zammad screens like the "
"dashboard, overviews, knowledge base or phone screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Content Tabs : You can find tabs for your opened tickets, users and "
"organizations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:64
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bottom Bar\n"
": Profile settings and create new ticket button. In case you have additional "
"permissions, there might be a settings and\n"
"  a reporting button as well.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:67
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad immediately saves your current work progress, so you can easily "
"switch between the different areas of Zammad and you don't have to be afraid "
"of losing any data like a not yet sent answer in a ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The sidebar on the right side displays all ticket relevant information and "
"includes additional functionality. The most important one is the ticket "
"sidebar. Switch between the different sidebars by clicking the desired tab "
"on the right side of the sidebar. The available tabs depend on the ticket "
"and the configured features of your Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<!-- markdownlint-disable MD007 -->\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ticket Tab\n"
": This tab shows the ticket information like owner, group, priority and "
"state and lets you edit these values.\n"
"  Additionally, the following actions are available when you click on the "
"::a:: button in the top section:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"History: shows a dialog with the history in the current ticket. This is "
"where you can find when and what actions was performed and by whom."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Merge: merge the ticket with another one in case a customer emailed you "
"multiple times about the same issue."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:84
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change customer: set another customer for the ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Customer Tab\n"
": View customer details including a reference to the customer’s other "
"tickets. You can change the ticket customer here\n"
"  as well by clicking on the ::a:: button in the top section.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/basics/zammad-ui.md:91
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Organization Tab\n"
": This tab is only shown if the customer is member of an organization. It "
"shows the organization’s details including all\n"
"  members. By clicking on the ::a:: button in the top section, you can edit "
"the organization.\n"
msgstr ""

