#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:1 src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "[[TOC]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:13 src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:8
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:92 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:244
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:361
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to find tickets?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It depends on your use case. Zammad offers many possibilities to search and "
"access tickets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you **search for a specific ticket or content**, the search is the best "
"way. You can find the search field in the top area of the navigation sidebar "
"or activate it by using the keyboard shortcut [[s]]. The search even shows "
"the tickets you recently closed from your taskbar, maybe you can already "
"find what you are searching for there. There is a separate [search "
"page](./guides/search) for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to **start working on tickets**, take a look at [the "
"overviews](./guides/overviews), which are basically a list of current "
"tickets. These overviews should put you in a position where you can easily "
"distinguish between what needs to be done, what is in progress and what is "
"currently on hold. In case you face issues with these overviews, your Zammad "
"admin should be able to help."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to get notified for ticket changes?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Adjust the [notification settings in your "
"profile](user-profile#notifications). You can distinguish between the action "
"(e.g. ticket creation), the notification channel (email and/or browser), "
"your relation to the ticket (e.g. if you are the owner) and limit the "
"notifications to a specific group."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:35
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Why is the ticket open again? I closed it already"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the settings of your Zammad instance, the reasons can "
"differ. But usually the reason is that a customer replied to the ticket "
"after it was set to closed. Another reason could be that a colleague "
"re-opened it. If you can't see an article which fits to the description, you "
"can take a look at the ticket history to find out more. Do so by opening the "
"::a:: menu in the ticket sidebar tab and select **History**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Your Zammad admin can adjust what should happen when a customer replies "
"after a ticket got closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What does the customer see in the ticket?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, customers only have a reduced interface. They can create "
"tickets, view their own tickets (and maybe their colleague's too, depending "
"on the setting) and access their profile settings. Even the ticket detail "
"view only includes relevant elements for the customer. Elements, which have "
"an internal purpose (like group, priority, internal notes, are not visible "
"to the customer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The explanation above is based on the default Zammad settings. Be aware that "
"the configuration of your system might be\n"
"different. If in doubt, you should ask your admin.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:56
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "I can't log in. What can I do?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Forgot your password? Try resetting it in the login screen under the "
"**Forgot password?** link by providing your email address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Lost the possibility to provide your 2nd factor for 2-factor-authentication "
"(2FA)? Use a recovery code and set up a new 2FA method. See [2FA "
"page](./guides/two-factor-auth) for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Lost your 2FA recovery codes? Get in touch with your Zammad admin. This also "
"applies if your problem is not mentioned here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How can I use keyboard shortcuts?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Just use them! You can find an overview of the available shortcuts by "
"pressing [[?]] on your keyboard or open the overview from the [avatar "
"menu](user-profile#avatar-menu) (click on your avatar in the bottom left "
"corner and select **Keyboard shortcuts**)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Some of them depend on the location you are or action you perform "
"(e.g. being in the editor or in the ticket detail view)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:74
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to switch between dark and light mode for the user interface?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can switch between light, dark and automatic mode (tries to adapt to "
"your browser) in the [avatar menu](user-profile#avatar-menu). Open it by "
"clicking your avatar in the bottom left corner and switch the toggle to the "
"desired state or use the keyboard shortcut [[d]]. If no input field is "
"activated, it cycles between the different modes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:81
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User Profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:83
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to change my profile/avatar image?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:88
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Go to the [avatar section](user-profile#avatar) in you profile settings by "
"opening the avatar menu in the bottom left corner and select **Profile "
"settings**. There you can upload an image, capture a photo (if your device "
"has a camera) or delete already present images."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:89
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to change the language of the Zammad user interface?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Go to the [language section](user-profile#language) in you profile settings "
"by opening the avatar menu in the bottom left corner and select **Profile "
"settings**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:94
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What should I do before going on vacation?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:98
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Go to the [out of office section](user-profile#out-of-office) in you profile "
"settings by opening the avatar menu in the bottom left corner and select "
"**Profile settings**. There you can define a replacement agent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to adjust the order of the overviews?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid "Read on in the [overview guide](guides/overviews#reorder-overviews)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:103
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Work on Tickets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:105
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to assign somebody to a ticket?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:109
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the ticket sidebar tab, you can find an **Owner** field. Choose from the "
"offered agents and make sure to leave an internal note so the other agent "
"knows what it is about."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you only have a question or need some information, you could also just "
"[mention a colleague](advanced-features#mention-a-colleague) in an article "
"by using [[@]][[@]] and raise your question."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:113
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to delete a ticket?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:118
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"First of all, tickets can't be deleted by agents. This is done for the "
"reason of transparency and to prevent deletion by accident and arbitrary "
"deletion. However, if customers want their data to be deleted (e.g. due to a "
"GDPR deletion request), this can be done in Zammad. Contact your Zammad "
"admin and ask to execute the deletion job."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:119
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to use text templates?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use Zammad's [text modules](advanced-features#text-modules) by typing "
"[[:]][[:]] in the article editor or choose it from the editor toolbar. If "
"you need to have additional modules, ask your Zammad admin to add it for "
"you."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:124
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to ask a colleague for help in the ticket?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:129
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The best way to do this is to [mention a "
"colleague](advanced-features#mention-a-colleague) in an article by using "
"[[@]][[@]] and raise your question. This triggers a notification for your "
"colleague. Depending on your internal processes, switching the owner of the "
"ticket could also be a possible option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:130
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to cite the customer's email or parts of it?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:134
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To partially or selective cite the article or parts of it, mark the text, "
"you want to cite, and click on the `Reply` button next to the article. This "
"can be done even multiple times (e.g. to answer different parts of the "
"ticket)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:136
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The citation of the whole article depends on how your Zammad is "
"configured. If you want to apply changes to this behavior, ask your admin to "
"change it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "AI Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad is getting even smarter! We are expanding Zammad's AI capabilities to "
"help you manage support tickets even more efficiently. ✨🚀"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The AI features have to be configured and activated by your "
"administrator. If you can't see it, it is not configured.\n"
"More information about how to configure and activate it can be found in the "
"admin section.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:18
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/ticket-summary.md:1
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/ticket-summary.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket Summary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The ticket summary feature does what it says: it summarizes the ticket's "
"content. This can be a huge time saver when dealing with large tickets "
"and/or many hand-overs between agents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the feature is activated, a summary of the ticket is generated when the "
"ticket got updated and you either open the ticket or open the summary "
"sidebar tab of the ticket, depending on the configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows Zammad's ticket detail view with highlighted ticket "
"summary banner and summary "
"sidebar](/screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-ai.cy.js/ai-ticket-summary-sidebar.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the configuration of your Zammad instance, the summary includes "
"the following sections:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Customer intent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Conversation summary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open questions (optional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Upcoming events (optional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Customer sentiment (optional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Writing Assistant Tools"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The AI-powered writing assistant tools are designed to simplify and enhance "
"your ticket response workflow while you create an article.  To use such a "
"tool, you first have to select text you want to apply the changes to. After "
"that, click the `Writing Assistant Tools` button at the left side of the "
"editor toolbar and choose one of the following tools, depending on what you "
"want to perform."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:45
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows Zammad's smart editor "
"menu](/screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-ai.cy.js/ai-writing-assistant-tools.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"- Be aware that your text gets replaced when you select one of the text "
"tools. If you are not satisfied with the result,\n"
"  try using the undo feature by pressing [[ctrl]] + [[z]].\n"
"- Always double-check the response. Although the feature was carefully "
"developed, there may still be minor problems in\n"
"  individual cases due to the nature of neural networks.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad ships default writing assistant tools. The availability depends on "
"the configuration of your Zammad instance. You might even have additional "
"custom tools in case your admin added them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Expand draft into well-written section**: Uses your draft as a base and "
"tries to elaborate a proper text. It tries to add a structure and to enhance "
"clarity and conciseness and as well as removing misspellings and grammar "
"errors. You can even use it by providing only basic information (e.g. via "
"bullet points) and let the AI write the answer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Fix spelling and grammar**: Proofreads your text and removes spelling and "
"grammar mistakes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Summarize section to about half its current size**: Shrinks your text "
"while keeping the message and the tone of the text."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"**Rewrite complex section and make it easy to understand**: Removes "
"unnecessary parts and rewrites your text in a clear and understandable way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "AI Agents"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/ai.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"AI agents can be configured to work on certain types of routine tasks. In "
"general, this feature operates behind the scenes but if configured, you may "
"notice it in some situations (see examples below). In case your admin "
"created a macro with an AI agent action, you can even run it manually. Ask "
"your admin for details and have a look at the [macro "
"description](/en/documentation/use/advanced-features#macros) in the advanced "
"features page."
msgstr ""

