#, markdown-text
msgid "2 normal: blue"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid "3 high: red"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:72
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Open a Ticket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:77
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Open a ticket by simply clicking on the line. This opens the ticket as a tab "
"in the left navigation bar and shows you the ticket detail view. If this "
"ticket is already present in your navigation bar, it activates this tab "
"instead of opening a duplicate tab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If an overview contains more than one ticket and you open one of the "
"tickets, you can find arrows in the ticket detail view header to switch to "
"the next/previous ticket of this overview."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Perform bulk actions by selecting multiple tickets and either use the "
"drop-down fields or drag them with the mouse to invoke the bulk action "
"overlay. You can find more information about that in the [Bulk "
"Actions](../advanced-features#bulk-actions) section in the advanced features "
"page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reorder Overviews"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the order of the overviews doesn't reflect your working process or you "
"just like to have a different order, you can re-arrange them for your "
"account. Use the `reorder items` button at the very top of the second level "
"navigation bar, which opens your [profile "
"settings](/en/documentation/use/user-profile#overviews) where you can define "
"a custom order for your overviews."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To change the order, simply drag & drop them by clicking the handles on the "
"left side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/overviews.md:97
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your admin changes the order, your custom order is preserved. You can "
"switch back to your admin's order by clicking the `Reset Overview Order` "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you search for tickets, user and organizations, you can use the "
"search. It is located in the top left corner in the primary navigation "
"bar. Either select it via mouse or use the keyboard shortcut [[s]]. Zammad "
"returns all fitting items for which you have at least view or read "
"permissions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows search results in navigation "
"bar](/screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-search.cy.js/search-sidebar.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The search covers basically all information which is stored in Zammad and "
"which got [indexed by Elasticsearch](/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes), "
"like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Message subject and text"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Names and email addresses"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "Text in file attachments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "User and organizations details (like notes, names, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When the search field gets activated, you can see the tickets which got "
"recently closed from your taskbar as well as your recent search queries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After entering a search term, you immediately see a preview of the search "
"results. These results are separated by type to make sure you won't get lost "
"in the results. Selecting one of those results will open a new navigation "
"tab (if not already opened) with the item."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you press [[enter]] or click on `detailed search`, Zammad displays a page "
"with search results. There you can narrow down your search by selecting a "
"specific object type (e.g. customer) in the tab bar below the search bar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows detailed "
"search](/screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-search.cy.js/search-detail.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are still facing many results, try to narrow down your search by "
"adding additional terms or use the sorting of the columns. To sort the "
"results based on the column's values, click on a column header. The sorting "
"is indicated by an arrow. Click on the column again to change the sorting "
"from ascending to descending and back. If you still can't find what you are "
"looking for, have a look at the next section where you can learn how to "
"search for specific attributes like creation date or the ticket owner's "
"email address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:42
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can narrow down your search results to specific attributes, even in the "
"search field in the navigation bar. Read on for some examples and "
"explanations. For a more detailed list of available attributes, please take "
"a look at the [indexed attributes by "
"Elasticsearch](/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid "Search for a ticket of a specific customer:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (plain)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "customer.firstname: John\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:57
#, markdown-text
msgid "or:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (plain)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "customer.lastname: Doe\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:62
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Combining Search Phrases"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can combine search phrases by using `AND`, `OR` and `TO` and even "
"separate them with `()`. If you want to exclude search results, you can use "
"negation `!`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Search phrase                                                                                 "
"| Description                                                                                                       "
"|\n"
"|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| `state.name:(closed OR open) AND (priority.name:\"2 normal\" OR "
"tags:feedback)`                 | Show every ticket that state is either "
"closed or open and has priority normal or the tag feedback.                "
"|\n"
"| `state.name:(closed OR open) AND (priority.name:\"2 normal\" OR "
"tags:feedback) AND !(_Zammad_)` | This gets the same result as above, expect "
"that we don't want the ticket to contain anything matching to \"Zammad\".|\n"
"| `owner.email:bob@example.net AND state.name:(open OR new)`                                    "
"| Show tickets with owner `bob@example.net` that are either open or new.                                            "
"|\n"
"| `state.name:pending* AND article_count: [1 TO 5]`                                             "
"| Show everything with any pending state and an article count of 1 to 5.                                            "
"|\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:74
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Additional Examples"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:84
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Attribute     | Examples                                                                                          "
"| Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          "
"|\n"
"|---------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| number        | `number:1118566`, `number:11185*`                                                                 "
"| Search for a specific ticket number.                                                                                                                                                                                                                 "
"|\n"
"| title         | `title:\"some title\"`, `title:Printer`, `title: \"some "
"ti*\"`                                        | If you need to use a space "
"in the search phrase, use quotes. Zammad combines the search terms with an "
"AND operator. You can also use a single keyword without quotation.                                                                             "
"|\n"
"| created_at    | `created_at:2018-11-18`, `created_at:[2018-11-15 TO "
"2018-11-18]`, `created_at:>now-1h`            | You can either use a simple "
"date, a date-range or `>now-xh`. Please note that the date format needs to "
"be `YYYY-MM-DD`.                                                                                                                              "
"|\n"
"| state.name    | `state.name: new`, `state.name:new OR open`, "
"`state.name:closed`                                  | You can filter for "
"specific ticket states (and even combine them with an OR). Please note that "
"you need to use the English names for states, unless you have custom ticket "
"states defined in your instance.                                          "
"|\n"
"| article_count | `article_count:5`, `article_count: [5 TO 10]`, "
"`article_count:[5 TO *]`, `article_count:[* TO 5]` | You can search for "
"Tickets with a specific number of articles (you can even search for "
"everything with 5 or more articles or up to 5 articles, if needed).                                                                                           "
"|\n"
"| article.from  | `article.from:*bob*`                                                                              "
"| Show all tickets that contain articles from a user with \"bob\" in its "
"name.                                                                                                                                                                           "
"|\n"
"| article.body  | `article.body:heat`, `article.body:heat~`, "
"`article.body:/joh?n(ath[oa]n)/`                       | First example shows "
"every ticket containing the word \"heat\" - you can also use the fuzzy "
"operator `~` to search for similar words like e.g. like \"head\". Zammad "
"will also allow you to use regular expressions, where ever the attributes "
"allows it. |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:1
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:6
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:72
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Two-Factor Authentication"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Two-factor authentication (2FA) enhances the security of your Zammad account "
"by adding an extra layer of verification beyond a password. It requires you "
"to provide two different types of authentication factors, typically "
"something you know (like a password) and something you possess (like a "
"mobile device or a security token), to ensure that you are an authorized "
"individual who can access the account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Two-Factor Authentication is an **optional feature**. Administrators must "
"activate it to be visible in your profile settings. The 2FA usage may be "
"even enforced by your admin. In this case, you can't use Zammad unless you "
"set up at least one 2FA method."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the system admin has enabled this feature, you can head to _Avatar > "
"Profile > Two-factor Authentication_ to set it\n"
"up. Depending on the enabled two-factor methods, you may see one or more "
"options in the table.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "To set up a two-factor method, use the ::+:: button and follow the steps."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows 2FA methods in user profile "
"settings](/screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-2fa.cy.js/2fa-methods-profile-setup.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "In a modal dialog, you will be asked to confirm your current password."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Depending on the chosen two-factor method, you will be guided through the "
"setup process, which includes specific steps.  Continue with using an "
"[Authentication App](#authentication-app) or a [Security "
"Key](#security-key)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication App"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The authenticator app method is a type of two-factor authentication that "
"uses a mobile application to generate one-time codes for account "
"verification. After setting up the authenticator app on your device, you "
"will link it to your Zammad account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows app authentication "
"configuration](/screenshots/two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-app-setup.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"First, make sure you have installed an authenticator app on your mobile "
"device. Recommended apps are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Google Authenticator](https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/1066447)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "[Authy](https://support.authy.com/hc/en-us/articles/115001945848-Installing-Authy-apps/)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[Microsoft "
"Authenticator](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/account-billing/download-and-install-the-microsoft-authenticator-app-351498fc-850a-45da-b7b6-27e523b8702a)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:47
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Next, open the authenticator app on your device and find a **Scan QR Code** "
"action, or similar. Point your camera to the Zammad screen and scan the "
"shown QR code in the middle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your device is not able to scan the QR code, first click on it to reveal "
"your secret. Next, add a manual entry to\n"
"your authenticator app and enter the provided secret when asked.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Your authenticator app should immediately add the new entry for your Zammad "
"account, and a 6-digit code will be displayed next to it together with a "
"timer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Back in Zammad, enter the provided code to the **Security Code** field and "
"click on **Set Up**. Go on either by setting up another 2FA method "
"([security key](#security-key)) or check how to [log in with 2FA](#sign-in)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Security Key"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The security keys method is a type of a two-factor authentication that uses "
"Web Authentication API in the browser for verifying your identity. You may "
"register multiple hardware or software security keys with your Zammad "
"account and then they can be used during the sign-in process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Initially, you will be presented with an empty side panel instructing you to "
"**Set Up** your first key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows security key authentication "
"configuration](/screenshots/two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-security-key-panel.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Then, enter a descriptive **Name for this security key** you will be "
"registering with your account, so you could later identify it in the "
"list. Then, click on **Next**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Next, depending you your browser, you will be presented with different "
"options. Select one that refers to your chosen security key and follow the "
"instructions on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows security key authentication "
"configuration](/screenshots/two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-passkey-auth.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You may be asked by the browser to interact with a key or a device so you "
"can prove you are in physical possession of it (e.g. enter its PIN to unlock "
"it)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You will have limited time (measured in tens of seconds) to register your "
"key. Better to have it ready before you\n"
"proceed!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the registration was successful, the modal dialog will close and you are "
"good to go. In case of errors, you will be able to **Retry** the "
"registration of the key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:89
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Once set up, security keys can be managed by choosing **Edit** action next "
"to the two-factor authentication method."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You have an option to remove a key or set up additional ones. There is no "
"limit in number of security keys you can set up, but keep in mind you cannot "
"register an already registered key for your account. Removal of the last "
"security key will effectively remove the complete security keys method for "
"your account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:94
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sign-in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:99
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When you set up two-factor authentication for your Zammad account, during "
"the next sign-in you will be asked to provide the same two-factor method "
"after entering correct username and password. Depending on the chosen "
"two-factor method, this may be a security code, hardware key, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you are having issues during sign-in with your preferred two-factor "
"authentication method, you can switch to another one, provided you have set "
"it up previously."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:105
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Look for **Try another method** link below the sign in box. In case you "
"don't see this link, you probably have no other available two-factor methods "
"set up, or your admin has disabled this feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Log in screen with link to \"Try another "
"method\"](/screenshots/two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-link-another-method.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:111
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also use one of your recovery codes, which are "
"auto-generated for your account during the initial setup of the two-factor "
"authentication. Click on **Or use one of your recovery codes**, enter one of "
"your unused codes and click on **Sign in**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Log in screen with recovery codes "
"link](/screenshots/two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-login-recovery-codes.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use a single recovery code only once! In case you exhaust the list "
"of your recovery codes, it is recommended\n"
"you regenerate them for your account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:119
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate Recovery Codes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Recovery codes are one-time use security codes that can be used to sign in "
"if you lose access to your other two-factor authentication methods. They can "
"only be used as a **backup method**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:126
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If the feature is enabled by the admin, recovery codes will be automatically "
"generated for you during the setup of your initial two-factor authentication "
"method."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:129
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You will be asked to print out or save the generated recovery codes in a "
"safe place. Once used, a recovery code cannot be reused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:131
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows output of recovery codes during 2FA "
"setup](/screenshots/two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-app-setup-recovery-codes.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You also have an option to regenerate your recovery codes at any time, which "
"invalidates already existing recovery codes and provides you with a list of "
"fresh codes. You can do this by clicking on `Regenerate recovery codes` "
"button in your profile's 2FA settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:136
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set a Default 2FA Method"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:140
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To set an already set up two-factor method as default, use the ::a:: actions "
"menu next to it in your profile's 2FA settings and choose **Set as "
"default**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:143
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In order to identify your current default two-factor authentication method, "
"look for a small blue badge next to the method name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:145
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows list of 2FA methods and default "
"method](/screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-2fa.cy.js/2fa-methods-profile-overview.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:148
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A default two-factor authentication method is just your preferred method "
"during the sign-in process. You will always have an option to try signing in "
"using another method."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:149
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Edit a 2FA Method"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
