#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Out of Office"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Define absence periods (e.g. for your vacation) and designate a substitute "
"to handle your tickets while you are away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:66
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Your designated substitute will receive updates on new tickets and changes "
"to existing ones while you're away.  Additionally, your custom overviews are "
"available for this agent to keep track of your tickets. You receive "
"notifications while you are absent, too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Password"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change the password of your account. To update it, provide your old "
"password, the new password and confirm the new one by typing it again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:76
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Set up a two-factor authentication (2FA) to increase the security of your "
"account. Your admin must have activated at least one 2FA method. It may be "
"even enforced to use a 2FA method by your admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:79
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After following the [2FA guide](./guides/two-factor-auth), you have to "
"provide your second factor at the next login.  If you can't provide your "
"configured 2FA method, contact your admin to reset it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:80
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Devices"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:85
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Here you can find a list of all devices logged into your Zammad account. If "
"necessary, you can revoke the access by clicking the delete icon in the "
"\"Actions\" column. This ends the session on this device and requires a new "
"login on this device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:86
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Token Access"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Generate a personal access token for a third party application to access the "
"Zammad API. After clicking the `New Personal Access Token` button, you can "
"set a name, an expiration date and configure the permissions for this token."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After creating the token, it gets displayed in a dialog only once. Make sure "
"to copy it because there is no possibility to access it again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows side panel with created token and copy "
"button](/screenshots/cypress/user-profile.cy.js/token-dialog.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:99
#, markdown-text
msgid "Adjust the notifications you get. You can adjust:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:105
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For which ticket actions you get notified (e.g. for new tickets, for "
"escalated tickets)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:105
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For which ticket you get notified based on the assignment and your relation "
"to it (e.g. only yours, not assigned, subscribed tickets)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:105
#, markdown-text
msgid "On which way you get notified (only in browser or additionally via email)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:105
#, markdown-text
msgid "For tickets in which group you get notified"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid "Additionally, you can select a notification sound or disable it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get notified via sound and notification on your operating system, you "
"have to allow Zammad to send you notifications.\n"
"This is requested when Zammad tries to send you a notification the first "
"time.\n"
"\n"
"If you refused it and want to allow it now, look for an icon in the address "
"bar where you can adjust the permissions of\n"
"the site. It depends on your web browser, how to do it exactly. If you can't "
"find it, search for it in the web or have\n"
"a look at your browser's settings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:122
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change the order of overviews for your account. Simply drag & drop them by "
"clicking the handles on the left side.  If your admin changes the order, "
"your custom order remains. You can switch back to your admin's order by "
"clicking the `Reset Overview Order` button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:123
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/calendar.md:1
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/calendar.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Calendar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/user-profile.md:128
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad allows you to subscribe to a calendar feed (ical) to see tickets in "
"your favorite calendar application.  Use either the upper **Combined "
"subscription URL** to subscribe to all tickets or the lower **Direct "
"subscription URL**.  By choosing the latter, you can define which tickets "
"based on ticket you want to include based on the state and assignment "
"status."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "> General Data Protection Regulation\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:10
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad GmbH Privacy Policy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This privacy policy describes how your personal information is collected, "
"used and shared when you visit <https://www.zammad.org> (the \"site\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Personal information we collect"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When you visit the site, we automatically collect certain information about "
"your device, including information about your web browser, IP address, time "
"zone, and some of the cookies that are installed on your "
"device. Additionally, as you browse the site, we collect information about "
"the individual web pages you view, what websites or search terms referred "
"you to the site, and information about how you interact with the site. We "
"refer to this automatically collected information as \"device information.\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "We collect device information using the following technologies:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"- \"Cookies\" are data files that are placed on your device or computer and "
"often include an anonymous unique identifier. For more information about "
"cookies and how to disable cookies visit <https://www.allaboutcookies.org>.  "
"- \"Log files\" track actions occurring on the site, and collect data "
"including your IP address, browser type, internet service provider, "
"referring/exit pages, and date/time stamps.  - \"Web beacons\", \"tags\", "
"and \"pixels\" are electronic files used to record information about how you "
"browse the site."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Use of Matomo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This website uses Matomo (formerly Piwik), an open source software for "
"statistical analysis of visitor access. Matomo uses cookies, which are text "
"files placed on your computer, to help us analyze how users use the site.  "
"The information generated by the cookie about your use of the website is "
"stored on a server in Germany. The IP address is made anonymous immediately "
"after processing and before it is stored. You have the option of preventing "
"the installation of cookies by changing the setting of your browser "
"software. We would like to point out that with the appropriate settings not "
"all functions of this website may be available to you anymore. You can "
"decide whether a unique web analysis cookie may be stored in your browser to "
"enable the operator of the website to collect and analyze various "
"statistical data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When we talk about \"personal information\" in this privacy policy, we are "
"talking both about device information and order information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How we use your personal information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:60
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We use the device information that we collect to help us screen for "
"potential risk and fraud (in particular, your IP address), and more "
"generally to improve and optimize our site (for example, by generating "
"analytics about how our customers browse and interact with the site, and to "
"assess the success of our marketing and advertising campaigns)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sharing your personal information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:64
#, markdown-text
msgid "We don't share your personal information with third parties."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:68
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We may share your personal information to comply with applicable laws and "
"regulations, to respond to a subpoena, search warrant or other lawful "
"request for information we receive, or to otherwise protect our rights."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Do not track"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please note that we do alter/reduce our site's data collection if we see a "
"\"Do Not Track\" signal from your browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:74
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Your rights"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:80
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are a European resident you have the right to access personal "
"information we hold about you and to ask that your personal information be "
"corrected, updated, or deleted. If you would like to exercise this right, "
"please contact us through the contact information below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:86
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Additionally, if you are a European resident we are processing your "
"information in order to fulfil contracts we might have with you (for example "
"if you make an order through the site), or otherwise to pursue our "
"legitimate business interests listed above. Additionally, please note that "
"your information will be transferred outside of Europe, including to Canada "
"and the United States."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Data retention"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:95
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We adhere to the principles of data avoidance and data economy. We therefore "
"only store your personal data for as long as is necessary to achieve the "
"purposes stated here or as provided for in the various storage periods "
"provided for by law. After the respective purpose or expiry of these "
"periods, the corresponding data will be blocked or deleted as a matter of "
"routine and in accordance with statutory regulations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Changes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:101
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"We may update this privacy policy from time to time in order to reflect, for "
"example, changes to our practices or for other operational, legal or "
"regulatory reasons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/gdpr.md:102
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Contact us"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:107
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For more information about our privacy practices, if you have questions, or "
"if you would like to make a complaint, please contact us by email at "
"<info@zammad.org> or by mail using the details provided below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/gdpr.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "Marienstraße 18, Berlin, BE, 10117, Germany"
msgstr ""

