#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Customizing the Zammad Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The Zammad stack can be customized by loading additional scenario files for "
"common use cases. For example, you can deploy the stack with an included "
"Nginx Proxy Manager (NPM) or with disabled PostgreSQL or Elasticsearch "
"services, in case you already have these services running."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:116
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please see the [Docker Compose scenarios "
"page](/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:118
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To adjust the stack and settings, use [Docker specific environment "
"variables](/en/reference/environment-variables)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:119
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to Run Commands in the Stack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Execute commands in your Docker stack by calling `rails` or `rake` via one "
"of the following methods by using `bundle exec`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Via Portainer GUI\n"
"\n"
"In your Portainer GUI, go to the container view and select the running Rails "
"container from your Zammad stack. Click\n"
"on the **Exec Console** icon in the \"Quick Actions\" column, select the "
"standard `/bin/bash` entrypoint and click\n"
"**Connect**.\n"
"\n"
"![Portainer console "
"execution](/screenshots/installation/portainer-exec-console.png){width=80%}\n"
"\n"
"Run the interactive Rails console by executing:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"bundle exec rails c\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Directly execute a specific command:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"bundle exec rails r '...your rails command here...'\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== Via console\n"
"\n"
"Directly execute a specific command:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver bundle exec rails r '...your "
"rails command here...'\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Run the interactive Rails console to manually enter Rails commands:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker compose run --rm zammad-railsserver bundle exec rails c\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Via `docker compose exec`:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"docker compose exec zammad-railsserver bundle exec rails r '...your rails "
"command here...'\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|tip)
#: src/en/get-started/installation/docker.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you need to retrieve information from the Rails server, you can, for "
"example,\n"
"place `pp` (pretty print) in front of your Rails command. This leads to an\n"
"output in your terminal.\n"
msgstr ""

