#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:1
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configure Database Server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This page should only enlighten the relevant parts for Zammad and is not "
"meant to be a complete guide. It is only relevant for you if you are running "
"an existing PostgreSQL server and want to run Zammad's database there as "
"well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you use database connection pooling software like PgBouncer, make sure to "
"use a pooling mode that is fully\n"
"compatible with PostgreSQL. Typically this is called \"session connection "
"pooling\". Transaction-based connection pooling\n"
"is not supported and may lead to errors during database migrations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Below you can the locations of the relevant PostgreSQL configuration files "
"to adjust. Keep in mind that versions may differ from your setup - adapt "
"where needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian & Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```ansi\n"
"/etc/postgresql/{your version}/main/postgresql.conf\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS & OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"```ansi\n"
"/var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== Others\n"
"\n"
"Can't find your configuration files? You can run the following command to "
"get the path:\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"sudo -u postgres psql -c 'SHOW config_file'\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adjust Pool Size"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Within `database.yml` (`config/` directory) you can define the allowed pool "
"size. By default each Zammad process takes up to `50` connections (`pool: "
"50`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This should be fairly enough for _every_ use case. If you experience "
"database connection timeouts or similar pool errors, this usually indicates "
"to other issues that are relevant to your PostgreSQL."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adjust `max_connections` (mandatory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad uses up to 200 connections by default. Depending on your setup and "
"load, you may want to change this value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:56
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Determine Value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To help you determine a number, Zammad ships a function to calculate a "
"suggestion. If executed, it asks you to input some integer values and "
"additionally uses internally known values for the calculation. Be aware that "
"the suggestion is instance specific. That means you must run the calculation "
"on the system you want to adjust the `max_connection` value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "Run it by using the command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:db:max_connections\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adjust Value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:71
#, markdown-text
msgid "Raise maximum allowed number of connections:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sed -i \"/max_connections/c\\max_connections = 2000\" "
"<postgresql-configuration-file>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:77
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:108
#, markdown-text
msgid "Apply changes by restarting PostgreSQL and Zammad (in this order):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:78
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo systemctl restart postgresql zammad\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:82
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adjust PostgreSQL for bigger instances (optional)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Check below settings first and ensure your system is able to provide the "
"requirements! Below settings are what we found\n"
"to be useful, everything else is out of scope of this documentation!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid "Some caching improvements:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:91
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sed -i \"/shared_buffers/c\\shared_buffers = 2GB\" "
"<postgresql-configuration-file>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sed -i \"/temp_buffers/c\\temp_buffers = 256MB\" "
"<postgresql-configuration-file>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "sed -i \"/work_mem/c\\work_mem = 10MB\" <postgresql-configuration-file>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/config-db-server.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sed -i \"/max_stack_depth/c\\max_stack_depth = 5MB\" "
"<postgresql-configuration-file>\n"
msgstr ""

