#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "General Usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Portainer\n"
"\n"
"Follow the [general deployment guide](/en/get-started/installation/docker) "
"and apply the following changes.\n"
"\n"
"Below the \"Compose path\" field, click on the `Add file` button. This opens "
"the \"Additional paths\" section where you\n"
"can specify the scenario you want to use. Add `scenarios/{scenario you want "
"to use}.yml` and replace the last part in\n"
"`{}` brackets with the name of one of the scenario files. You can even "
"combine the scenarios by adding additional paths.\n"
"\n"
"![Portainer additional paths "
"configuration](/screenshots/installation/portainer-additional-paths.png)\n"
"\n"
"=== Docker Compose\n"
"\n"
"Follow the first 2 steps of the [general deployment "
"guide](/en/get-started/installation/docker). To start the stack with\n"
"one or more additional scenarios, use the following command for step 3 in "
"the cloned repository folder instead:\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f scenarios/{scenario you want to "
"use}.yml up -d\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Replace the part in `{}` brackets with the file name of one of the scenario "
"files. You can even combine the scenarios\n"
"by adding additional files according to the example above.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Making the Stack Available via HTTPS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you set up Zammad for production use, it needs to be secured by using an "
"HTTPS connection. There are different scenarios for achieving this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Cloudflare Tunnel"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:69
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to publish Zammad in a very convenient way, you can use a "
"[Cloudflare](https://www.cloudflare.com/) tunnel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-cloudflare-tunnel.yml` for deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add a sub-domain to an already existing domain in your Cloudflare dashboard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Create a tunnel for this subdomain and configure it to forward traffic to "
"your zammad-nginx service with `http://zammad-nginx:8080`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Provide your Cloudflare tunnel token to the Zammad stack by using the "
"environment variable `CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Nginx Proxy Manager"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A very common setup of publishing web services is to use a reverse proxy, "
"which handles the SSL termination. One common tool is the Nginx Proxy "
"Manager (NPM), which can be configured via UI quite simply. If you don't "
"have a reverse proxy already, this might be a useful scenario for you. If "
"you already have a running reverse proxy, head over to the next section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid "Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-nginx-proxy-manager.yml` for deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid "Provide your FQDN for Zammad by using the environment variable `ZAMMAD_FQDN`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Configure your DNS. The chosen Zammad FQDN should point to the IP address of "
"the NPM host"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:87
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Configure a new proxy host in your NPM and follow the steps to get an SSL "
"certificate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add External Docker Network to Nginx"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:93
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you already have a reverse proxy which takes care about the SSL "
"termination, this scenario is helpful. It adds an external Docker network to "
"Zammad's included Nginx service to be able to access it from a reverse proxy "
"that is not part of the Zammad stack's network."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-external-network-to-nginx.yml` for "
"deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Provide the name of your external network by using the environment variable "
"`ZAMMAD_NGINX_EXTERNAL_NETWORK`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:97
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Using External Services"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Disable Elasticsearch Service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:103
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Do you have an Elasticsearch instance already running and want to use it for "
"Zammad, too? Then you can disable the Elasticsearch service in the Zammad "
"stack to save resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/disable-elasticsearch-service.yml` for "
"deployment - this will turn off the built-in service for Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the following environment variables to provide information about the "
"connection to your existing Elasticsearch instance:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_SCHEMA`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_HOST`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_PORT`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_USER`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:113
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ELASTICSEARCH_PASS`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:114
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Making Services Externally Available"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:118
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"These scenarios are meant to connect from external applications to Zammad "
"services. Depending on where your external service is hosted, you can use "
"one of the following scenarios."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"When exposing Elasticsearch outside the stack, make sure to set the variable "
"`ELASTICSEARCH_PASS` to a custom value\n"
"first! Otherwise this is a big security issue because the Elasticsearch "
"index contains most of Zammad's data.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:126
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"If you want to use TLS, you have to connect to Elasticsearch via reverse "
"proxy.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:132
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add External Docker Network to Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:137
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A common use case for this is to use a reporting/visualization tool like "
"Grafana on the same host in another stack.  Because such tools need to "
"access the Elasticsearch index, the network of the other stack has to be "
"added to Zammad's Elasticsearch container."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:140
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-external-network-to-elasticsearch.yml` "
"for deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:140
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Provide the name of your external network by using the environment variable "
"`ZAMMAD_ELASTICSEARCH_EXTERNAL_NETWORK`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:141
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Host Port to Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:145
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you want to expose the Elasticsearch service of the Zammad stack in "
"the network, you can assign a host port to the container. This is useful if "
"you need to access the Elasticsearch container from a different host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:149
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the scenario file `scenarios/add-hostport-to-elasticsearch.yml` for "
"deployment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:149
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The default port for Elasticsearch is `9200`. Change it to another port by "
"using the environment variable `ELASTICSEARCH_EXPOSE_HTTP_PORT`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:150
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Additional Scenarios"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:152
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Disable Backup Service"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:156
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you want to handle backups in a different way, you can disable the "
"built in backup service in the stack to save resources."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:158
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can do so by just using the scenario file "
"`scenarios/disable-backup-service.yml` for deployment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:159
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Ollama"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:162
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can spin up an additional [Ollama](https://ollama.com/) container to use "
"Zammad's AI features on your machine."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:163
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is intended for development or testing purposes as running a productive "
"LLM stack is complex.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:170
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To deploy an Ollama container inside the Zammad stack, use the scenario file "
"`scenarios/add-ollama.yml`. This creates an Ollama container which "
"automatically pulls and serves `Llama3.2` to be ready to use/test AI "
"features out of the box."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:172
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To use it in Zammad, add the service name and port (`http://ollama:11434`) "
"to the provider configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:173
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Limit Resources"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:179
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to limit the hardware resources the Zammad stack is allowed to "
"use, use the `scenarios/apply-resource-limits.yml` scenario. Default values "
"for CPU and memory usage for each container in the stack are applied "
"then. You can find these default values in the `.env.dist` file. Provide the "
"changed variables you want to use as environment variables and deploy the "
"stack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:180
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other Use Cases"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:184
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Your scenario is not covered yet? Feel free to suggest your use case. We "
"plan to add more common use cases to the stack in future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:185
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Customize the Stack Locally"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios.md:190
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's necessary to apply local changes to the Zammad Docker stack, "
"e.g. to include additional services. If you plan to do so, we recommend that "
"you do not change the `docker-compose.yml` file, but instead create a local "
"`docker-compose.override.yml` that includes all your modifications. Docker "
"Compose will [automatically load this file and merge its changes into your "
"stack](https://docs.docker.com/compose/multiple-compose-files/merge/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:1
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Find the most important environment variables below with default values (as "
"<Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"badge\" />), if\n"
"applicable. The variables for Docker and package based installations can be "
"different in some cases. You can find\n"
"another badge appended to variable names with the following meaning:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only available for Docker installations: ::d::"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only available for package installations: ::p::"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Available for both installation variants: without badge"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:16
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"If you want to use a `.env` file in Docker Compose deployments, you can use "
"the provided `.env.dist` file and copy it\n"
"to `.env`. That way it will be picked up by Docker Compose automatically and "
"not overwritten during updates.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:23
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Miscellaneous"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`GPG_PATH` ::p::\n"
": Defines the path of your GPG installation. Only needed if you want to use "
"different versions of PGP or if your PGP\n"
"  installation differs from the standard installation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`RAILS_LOG_TO_STDOUT` ::p::\n"
": This setting can be overwritten during update on package "
"installations. Use `enabled` to turn this option on only\n"
"  until the next update. Use `true` to turn it on permanently.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:36
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_SAFE_MODE` ::p::\n"
": Be careful when running Zammad commands on production systems in safe "
"mode. While it may allow an escape hatch for\n"
"  certain commands, it has a potential to break regular Zammad operations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_BIND_IP` ::p:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"127.0.0.1\" />\n"
": The IP address that the web server is bound to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`S3_URL` ::p::\n"
": Allows you to provide your S3 storage provider configuration. Example for "
"value:\n"
"  "
"`https://key:secret@s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/zammad-storage-bucket?region=eu-central-1&force_path_style=true`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`VERSION` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"current stable version of "
"Zammad\" />\n"
": Allows customization of the Zammad image tag. Example: `6.3.1-54`. This "
"default version may be increased when you\n"
"  update your Zammad Docker stack. Please see the\n"
"  [example env "
"file](https://github.com/zammad/zammad-docker-compose/blob/master/.env.dist) "
"for more details on this\n"
"  variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:56
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`AUTOWIZARD_JSON` ::d::\n"
": This variable allows you to provide initial configuration data for your "
"instance. Autowizard JSON is out of scope of\n"
"  this documentation, however\n"
"  [this example "
"file](https://github.com/zammad/zammad/blob/stable/contrib/auto_wizard_example.json) "
"should help.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_HTTP_TYPE` : Set the http type for your instance. Possible values "
"are `http` and `https`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:62
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ZAMMAD_FQDN` : Set the FQDN for your instance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`RAILS_TRUSTED_PROXIES` <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"127.0.0.1,::1\" />\n"
": This setting is important for the correct detection of client IP addresses "
"and features based on it, like rate\n"
"  limiting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:70
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  By default, Zammad trusts localhost proxies only. Any additional proxy "
"servers will have to be added here,\n"
"  by IP address (if static) or by host name. Host names are resolved during "
"the start of Zammad, so that a restart is\n"
"  required whenever the IP address of a proxy server changes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Note that in Docker context, Zammad may see the network   gateway IP "
"address instead of the actual proxy server\n"
"  IP address, if it is placed in another network.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:77
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_MANAGE_SESSIONS_JOBS_WORKERS` <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"0\" />\n"
": Allows to fork the job that dispatches the session jobs to their workers "
"to a child process. Allowed value to enable\n"
"  it: `1`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:83
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_AI_JOBS_WORKERS` <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"0\" />\n"
": Such a worker handles Zammad’s AI requests and fetches the responses from "
"the configured AI provider. This variable\n"
"  allows you to specify the number of workers to run simultaneously. `0` "
"means a thread in the main process is used, `1`\n"
"  means a separate worker gets spawned, etc. The maximum number of workers "
"is `16`. See also\n"
"  `ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_AI_JOBS_WORKERS_THREADS`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:86
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Self hosted AI users should be careful in increasing it, your AI service "
"might collapse. For AI cloud service users\n"
"  with a big Zammad instance, it could make sense to increase it to have "
"some kind of parallelization.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:91
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_AI_JOBS_WORKERS_THREADS` <Badge type=\"tip\" "
"text=\"5\" />\n"
": How many threads should be processed by a **single** AI worker (if you run "
"more than one worker process, it gets\n"
"  multiplied). This may speed up the AI processing, but be aware that a Ruby "
"worker can only span across 1 core anyway.\n"
"  The maximum number of threads is `16`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:96
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_COMMUNICATION_INBOUND_JOBS_WORKERS` <Badge "
"type=\"tip\" text=\"0\" />\n"
": Allows concurrent fetching of inbound communication channels. Useful if "
"you have many channels and/or mailboxes added.\n"
"  `0` means a thread in the main process is used, `1` means a separate "
"worker gets spawned, etc. The maximum number of\n"
"  workers is `16`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:100
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_COMMUNICATION_INBOUND_JOBS_WORKER_THREADS` <Badge "
"type=\"tip\" text=\"1\" />\n"
": Threads used for fetching inbound communication channels. How many threads "
"should be processed by a **single** inbound\n"
"  jobs worker (if you run more than one worker process, it gets "
"multiplied). The maximum number of threads is `16`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:104
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`MEMCACHE_SERVERS` <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"Docker: "
"zammad-memcached:11211\" /> <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"Package: unset\" />\n"
": Provide your own Memcached instance to Zammad if you already have one. The "
"package installation fallback is\n"
"  `/opt/zammad/tmp/cache*`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:108
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`REDIS_URL` <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"Docker: redis://zammad-redis:6379\" "
"/> <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"Package: unset\" />\n"
": Provide your own Redis instance if you already have one. The package "
"installation fallback is\n"
"  `/opt/zammad/tmp/websocket_*`. See [Redis Variables](/en/reference/redis) "
"for a Sentinel setup.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:109
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:114
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_ENABLED` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"true\" />\n"
": Setting this variable to false will allow you to run your Zammad without "
"Elasticsearch. Please note that we strongly\n"
"  advise **against** doing so.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:117
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_HOST` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad-elasticsearch\" "
"/>\n"
": Provide a host name or address to your external Elasticsearch cluster.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:120
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_PORT` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"9200\" />\n"
": Provide a different port for Elasticsearch if needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:123
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_SCHEMA` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"http\" />\n"
": Change it to `https` if your Elasticsearch cluster is configured to use "
"SSL.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:126
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_NAMESPACE` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad\" />\n"
": With this name space all Zammad related indexes will be created. Change "
"this if you're using external clusters.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:130
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_REINDEX` ::d::\n"
": The searchindex automatically gets rebuilt when no index can be "
"detected. If you need to rebuild the searchindex\n"
"  manually, either set this variable to `true` or run the reindex command "
"via Docker manually.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:134
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_SSL_VERIFY` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"true\" />\n"
": Allows you to let the Compose scripts ignore self signed SSL certificates "
"for your Elasticsearch installation if\n"
"  needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:138
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ELASTICSEARCH_HEAP_SIZE` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"1G\" />\n"
": Set the available memory for Elasticsearch. If you face issues with ES and "
"its performance, you should increase this\n"
"  value to a reasonable size.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:141
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Variables for Docker and package installation are partially different. Check "
"the limitation badge and make sure to pick\n"
"the right one. The both variables at the end of the list are valid for both "
"installation types.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:149
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_HOST` ::p:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad-postgresql\" />\n"
": Host name or IP address of your PostgreSQL server. In case you use an IPv6 "
"address, enclose the address in square\n"
"  brackets (e.g. `[2001:db8::2]`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:152
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_PORT` ::p:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"5432\" />\n"
": Adjust the port of your PostgreSQL server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:155
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_USER` ::p:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad\" />\n"
": The database user for Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:158
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_PASS` ::p:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad\" />\n"
": The password of Zammad's database user.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:161
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_DB` ::p:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad_production\" />\n"
": Zammad's database to use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:165
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRES_HOST` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad-postgresql\" />\n"
": Host name or IP address of your PostgreSQL server. In case you use an IPv6 "
"address, enclose the address in square\n"
"brackets (e.g. `[2001:db8::2]`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:168
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRES_PORT` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"5432\" />\n"
": Adjust the port of your PostgreSQL server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:171
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRES_USER` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad\" />\n"
": The database user for Zammad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:174
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRES_PASS` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad\" />\n"
": The password of Zammad's database user.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:177
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRES_DB` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad_production\" />\n"
": Zammad's database to use.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:180
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_OPTIONS` <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"?pool=50\" />\n"
": Additional PostgreSQL params to be appended to the database URI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:184
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`POSTGRESQL_DB_CREATE` <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"true\" />\n"
": By default, Zammad creates the required database. On already existing "
"database servers, the default might be\n"
"  troublesome.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:190
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_EXPOSE_PORT` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"8080\" />\n"
": The port to be exposed for accessing the Zammad stack from outside. Change "
"this to another value if you already have\n"
"  an existing service listening on this port.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:193
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_PORT` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"8080\" />\n"
": The internal port the Nginx service will listen on.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:196
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_SERVER_NAME` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"_\" />\n"
": By default, the Nginx container of Zammad will respond to all request. You "
"can provide your IP / FQDN if you want to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:201
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`NGINX_SERVER_SCHEME` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"\\$scheme\" />\n"
": If the Nginx container for Zammad **is not** the upstream server (aka "
"you're using another proxy in front of Nginx)\n"
"  `$scheme` may be wrong. You can set the correct scheme `http` or `https` "
"if needed. Set this if you face a\n"
"  `CSRF Token Verification Failed` error.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:204
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`NGINX_CLIENT_MAX_BODY_SIZE` ::d:: : Define the maximum size of data that a "
"client can send to the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:207
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILSSERVER_HOST` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" "
"text=\"zammad-railsserver\" />\n"
": Host name of the Rails server container.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:210
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILSSERVER_PORT` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"3000\" />\n"
": Port of Zammad's Rails server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:213
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_RAILS_PORT` ::p:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"3000\" />\n"
": Port of Zammad's Rails server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:216
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEBSOCKET_HOST` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"zammad-websocket\" "
"/>\n"
": Host name of Zammad's websocket server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:219
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEBSOCKET_PORT` ::d:: <Badge type=\"tip\" text=\"6042\" />\n"
": Port of Zammad's websocket server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:220
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Performance Tuning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:224
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Each of below settings comes with its own tradeoffs. There are no "
"recommended values here; the optimal configuration depends on your system's "
"resources and typical application load."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:227
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Proceed with caution; when adjusting any of these settings, there is a point "
"at which performance will begin to degrade rather than improve, or other "
"problems will begin to emerge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:230
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Below settings may consume all available database connections. Please "
"consider the [Configure Database Server](config-db-server) for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:235
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_WEB_CONCURRENCY`\n"
": Allows spawning `n` workers to allow more simultaneous connections for "
"Zammad's web UI. In case you applied\n"
"  [Docker hardware resource "
"limits](docker-compose-scenarios#limit-resources), the zammad-railsserver's "
"CPU setting\n"
"  should match the value from this variable.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:240
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_SESSION_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": How many processes of the session worker to run at a time. Increasing this "
"value can speed up background jobs (like\n"
"  the scheduler) when many users are on Zammad at once. However, it is not "
"useful to adjust this setting if you have\n"
"  less than 40 active users at a time. Increasing the amount of these "
"processes can consume a lot of resources!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:243
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:250
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:257
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In case you applied [Docker hardware resource "
"limits](docker-compose-scenarios#limit-resources), the zammad-scheduler\n"
"  CPU setting should match the sum of all worker settings variables.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:247
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_SCHEDULED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": Allows spawning `1` independent scheduled jobs worker to release pressure "
"from Zammad's background worker. Maximum\n"
"  number of workers: `1`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:254
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_JOBS_WORKERS`\n"
": Allows spawning `n` worker processes to release pressure from Zammad’s "
"background worker. `0` means a thread in the\n"
"  main process is used, `1` means a separate worker gets spawned, etc. The "
"maximum number of workers is `16`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:261
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`ZAMMAD_PROCESS_DELAYED_JOBS_WORKER_THREADS`\n"
": Threads used by **one** delayed jobs worker process (if you have more than "
"one worker process, it is multiplied by\n"
"  their amount). The maximum number of threads is `16`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:262
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How to Set Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/environment-variables.md:267
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"It depends on how you installed Zammad (package, Docker). Either set it via "
