#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a Request"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:70
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"All requests and responses are in JSON format. This means all information "
"must be encapsulated in brackets and have a hierarchical structure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:73
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Let's have a look at a request to fetch information from Zammad. Such a "
"request starts with the string `query`, followed by an object you want to "
"query."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "Basic example to fetch users with their first and last name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (gql :line-numbers)
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"query userName (\n"
"  $userId: ID!\n"
"  ) {\n"
"  user(userId: $userId) {\n"
"    firstname\n"
"    lastname\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:89
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The `$userId` from line 2 defines a variable which is used as an ID. In the "
"variables section of your client, provide the value for it. In this example, "
"the variables section looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (json)
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"userId\": \"gid://zammad/User/2\"\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:99
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The value above is in the global ID format of Zammad's GraphQL "
"implementation. Depending on which object type you want to deal with, "
"replace the `User` by another object like `Ticket`, `Organization`, `Group`, "
"etc. Zammad expects a numeric value as ID."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:102
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Starting with line 4 in the code block above is the actual request. This "
"simple example just fetches the attributes `firstname` and `lastname` from "
"the user with the ID 2."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:104
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Click on details to watch a screencast showing a basic request using a "
"variable in Bruno."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details)
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<video controls=\"controls\" "
"src=\"/public/videos/graphql-user-request-variable.mp4\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:110
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To create or change data, replace the `query` by `mutation` in the request "
"body."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/graphql.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The examples use variables for the different object types. Make sure to set "
"it when using the examples."
msgstr ""

