msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:161
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "User Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:163
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:167
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In order to work on user information or to check for specific information, "
"you'll need to find it first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:169
#, markdown-text
msgid "User ID already known:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find(4)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:175
#, markdown-text
msgid "Searching for the user by his email address:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:176
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(email: 'your@email')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:181
#, markdown-text
msgid "Searching for the user by his login:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:182
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(login: 'john.doe')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:186
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unlock a Locked User Account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:188
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlocking a locked user account is also supported by Zammad's web UI!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:196
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It sometimes happens that a user locks himself out by wildly trying the\n"
"wrong password multiple times. Depending on your maximum failing login\n"
"count (<span class=\"title-ref\">default: 10 times</span>), Zammad might\n"
"lock the account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:199
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The user can't login any more (forever) if he doesn't change the password or "
"you reset the counter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "u=User.find(**USERID**)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:204
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.login_failed=0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:208
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:237
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:256
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:275
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.save!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:215
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can also double check if the account is locked by running the following "
"command (result needs to be 1 above your limit, so 11 for the default of 10 "
"failing logins):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:216
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find(**USERID**).login_failed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:220
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change / Update Email Address of User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:223
#, markdown-text
msgid "If needed, you can simply change the email address of the user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:224
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Please note that the login attribute is not affected by this and\n"
"Zammad thus might show different information within the UI.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:229
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:248
#, no-wrap
msgid "u = User.find(**USERID**)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.email = 'user@exmaple.com'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:242
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:261
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need to find the user ID of the user first for this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:243
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change / Update Login Name of User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:247
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change the user name of the user (e.g. if you want to login with a shorter "
"username instead of a mail address)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:252
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.login = 'user@exmaple.com'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:262
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set Admin Rights for User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:266
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Don't have access to Zammad anymore? Grant yourself or another user "
"administrative rights."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:267
#, no-wrap
msgid "u = User.find_by(email: 'you@example.com')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "u.roles = Role.where(name: ['Agent', 'Admin'])\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:279
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set Password for User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You or the user did forget his password? No problem! Simply reset it by hand "
"if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:284
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"User.find_by(email: 'you@example.com').update!(password: "
"'your_new_password')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:288
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remove Password for User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:295
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you added a second authentication method (e.g. LDAP) after launch, there "
"still may be a password in Zammad's own user management. In cases like that "
"users will be able to login with their (local) Zammad password in addition "
"to the credentials stored on the external authentication provider. Simply "
"remove the password stored by Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:296
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(email: 'you@example.com').update!(password: nil)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:300
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Group Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:302
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find a Group"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group.find_by(name: 'Users').follow_up_possible\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:308
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Chat Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:310
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remove IP Address Logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:314
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use the following command to remove all IP address records from closed chats "
"that haven't been updated in the last seven days:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:315
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Chat::Session.where(state: 'closed').where('updated_at < ?', "
"7.days.ago).each do |session|\n"
"next if session.preferences['remote_ip'].blank?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:320
#, no-wrap
msgid "session.preferences.delete('geo_ip')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:324
#, no-wrap
msgid "session.preferences.delete('remote_ip')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:328
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"session.save!(touch: false)\n"
"end\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:333
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zammad Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:337
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In this section, you can find some settings which you can set in the Zammad "
"UI as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:338
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Auto Shutdown Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:345
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Defines if an automatic shutdown of Zammad is performed when the the "
"database has been changed (e.g. after custom attributes have been created in "
"the object manager).  The underlying system (Systemd, Docker, Kubernetes) "
"will then restart the processes/containers after this shutdown. The default "
"setting is `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:348
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Setting this to `false` might only make sense in very rare cases and you "
"have to restart the Zammad services then manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('auto_shutdown', 'true')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:353
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket_hook Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:358
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This will give you the ticket hook that you'll find inside the `[]` in front "
"of the ticket number. By default this will be `Ticket#` - you shouldn't "
"change this setting in a productive system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:359
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ticket_hook')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:363
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "FQDN Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:366
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current FQDN setting of Zammad and, if needed, adjust it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:367
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This setting has no effect on SSL certificates or any web server\n"
"configurations.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:373
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get current FQDN:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:374
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('fqdn')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:379
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set a new FQDN:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:380
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('fqdn', 'new.domain.tld')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:384
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP(s) Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:388
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This setting indirectly belongs to your FQDN setting and is relevant for "
"variable based URLs (e.g. in notifications) Zammad generated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:389
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This setting also affects Zammad's CSRF token behavior. If you set\n"
"this to e.g. HTTPs but you're using HTTP, logging in will\n"
"fail!\n"
"\n"
"It has no effect on SSL certificates or any web server configuration.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:398
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current http type:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:399
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('http_type')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:404
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change the http type to HTTPs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:405
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('http_type', 'https')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:409
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Storage Provider Setting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:415
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The storage provider setting is set to `DB` on default installations.  "
"However, if you receive a lot of attachments or have a fairly busy "
"installation, using the database to store attachments is not the best "
"approach."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:417
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current attachment storage:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:418
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('storage_provider')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:423
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change attachment storage to database"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:424
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('storage_provider', 'DB')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:433
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you have already stored files and want to move them, you can use the "
"following example. Please be aware that this operation should only be "
"executed in non-productive environments. In case you have to perform it in "
"production environments, you should specify a sleep delay - otherwise your "
"Zammad can be unresponsive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:435
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Move files from DB to File with a specified delay after each file in "
"seconds:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:436
#, no-wrap
msgid "Store::File.move('DB', 'File', delay_in_sec)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:441
#, markdown-text
msgid "The following settings are available in a default installation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:444
#, markdown-text
msgid "`DB` (database)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:444
#, markdown-text
msgid "`File` (Filesystem (`/opt/zammad/storage/`))"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:445
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configuring Elasticsearch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:449
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your Elasticsearch installation changes, you can use the following "
"commands to ensure that Zammad still can access Elasticsearch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:451
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change Elasticsearch URL:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:452
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('es_url', 'http://127.0.0.1:9200')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:457
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change Elasticsearch user (e.g. for authentication):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:458
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('es_user', 'elasticsearch')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:463
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change the Elasticsearch password for authentication:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:464
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('es_password', 'zammad')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:469
#, markdown-text
msgid "Change the index name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:470
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('es_index', Socket.gethostname + '_zammad')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:475
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ignore files by file extension from being indexed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:476
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setting.set('es_attachment_ignore', %w[.png .jpg .jpeg .mpeg .mpg .mov .bin "
".exe .box .mbox])\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:481
#, markdown-text
msgid "Limit the attachment size:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:482
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('es_attachment_max_size_in_mb', 50)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:487
#, markdown-text
msgid "Turn SSL verification on or off:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:488
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('es_ssl_verify', 'false')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:492
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Enable Proxy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:495
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set a proxy to use by Zammad:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:496
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('proxy', 'proxy.example.com:3128')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:500
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('proxy_username', 'some user')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:504
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('proxy_password', 'some pass')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:508
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Disable Asciifold"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:511
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This feature is turned on by default. In case you need a more exact search, "
"you can turn it off:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:512
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('es_asciifolding', false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:517
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After changing the setting, make sure to [rebuild the search "
"index](/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch#build-rebuild-the-searchindex)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:518
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hidden Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:523
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In this section you can find some settings that you won't find within the "
"Zammad UI. Those settings might come in handy as it can change Zammad's "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:524
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Send All Outgoing EMails to a BCC-Mailbox"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:530
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This option allows you to send all outgoing emails (not notifications)  to a "
"specific mailbox. Please note that this shouldn't be a mailbox you're "
"importing already! This will apply to all groups and is a global setting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:531
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('system_bcc', 'alias@domain.tld')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:536
#, markdown-text
msgid "You can easily check the current BCC-Setting by running the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:537
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('system_bcc')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:541
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate Counter on Grouped Overviews"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:544
#, markdown-text
msgid "This enables a ticket number value in each heading for grouped elements."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:546
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enable counter for grouped overviews:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:547
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_table_group_by_show_count', true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:552
#, markdown-text
msgid "Disable counter for grouped overviews:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:553
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_table_group_by_show_count', false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:558
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get current setting (`nil` is false):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:559
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ui_table_group_by_show_count')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:563
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Default Ticket Type on Creation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:567
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad allows you to define the default article type upon ticket "
"creation. By default this will be a incoming phone call."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:569
#, markdown-text
msgid "You can choose between"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:573
#, markdown-text
msgid "`phone-in` (incoming call, **default**),"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:573
#, markdown-text
msgid "`phone-out` (outgoing call) and"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:573
#, markdown-text
msgid "`email-out` (Sending an email out)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:574
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_ticket_create_default_type', 'email-out')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:579
#, markdown-text
msgid "To check what setting is set currently, simply run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:580
