#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:659
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_user_organization_selector_with_email', true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:664
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:684
#, markdown-text
msgid "Get the current state of this setting with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:665
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('ui_user_organization_selector_with_email')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:669
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Change Font Settings for Outgoing HTML Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:671
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some clients (like Outlook) might fallback to other settings while it\n"
"might work for other clients.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:678
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The below setting allows you to adjust Zammad's email font setting. This "
"setting does not require a service restart."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:679
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Setting.set(\"html_email_css_font\", \"font-family:'Helvetica Neue', "
"Helvetica, Arial, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:685
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.get('html_email_css_font')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:689
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Highlight Customer's Open Ticket Count"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:693
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This option enhances the selected customer's open tickets count. It "
"highlights the count in different colors if they hit a threshold."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:694
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_sidebar_open_ticket_indicator_colored', true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:700
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Above settings has specific thresholds as follows. You **cannot** adjust "
"these thresholds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:705
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Situation / View      | no indication | warning (orange) | danger (red) "
"|\n"
"|-----------------------|---------------|------------------|--------------|\n"
"| **Ticket Zoom**       | \\< 2          | 2                | \\>= 3        "
"|\n"
"| **New Ticket dialog** | 0             | 1                | \\>= 2        "
"|\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:706
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate Attachment Tab in Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:710
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This option activates a new tab in the right sidebar in the ticket view "
"which shows all attachments of the currently viewed ticket."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:711
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_ticket_zoom_sidebar_article_attachments', 'true')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:715
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Time Period for Showing Customer Profile on New Calls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:721
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad shows the customer profile dialog when a call of this customer is "
"incoming and there is an existing ticket of this customer in this time "
"period. The default time period is 30 days. If there is no ticket in this "
"period, the customer dialog is not shown automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:723
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set the time period to 90 days:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:724
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('cti_customer_last_activity', '90')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:728
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set Public \"Notes\" as SLA relevant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:734
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Normally, notes aren't SLA relevant. Use the following command to include "
"publicly-visible notes when tracking SLA compliance (internal notes _will "
"never_ affect SLA calculations). Be aware that this setting will disable the "
"option to delete public notes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:735
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, customers are not notified when public notes are added to a\n"
"ticket. Set up a trigger if you wish to change this behavior.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:741
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enable SLA to count notes as communication:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:742
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket::Article::Type.find_by(name:'note').update!(communication: true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:747
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enable SLA to ignore notes as communication:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:748
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket::Article::Type.find_by(name:'note').update!(communication: false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:752
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Activate Priority Icon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:756
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To activate additional icons which represent the priority, use the command "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:757
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ui_ticket_priority_icons', true)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:761
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Other Useful Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:763
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Remove AI Feature"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:767
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad's AI feature is completely optional and requires a configuration "
"before any AI request is made. However, if you don't want to see the "
"feature, you can do so by setting the permission to inactive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:769
#, markdown-text
msgid "Disable any AI provider, in case you already configured it:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:770
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting.set('ai_provider', false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:775
#, markdown-text
msgid "Disable permission to hide the settings from UI:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:776
#, no-wrap
msgid "Permission.where(\"name LIKE 'admin.ai%'\").update!(active: false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:781
#, markdown-text
msgid "To re-enable it, set the `active` flag to `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:782
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fetch Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:786
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The below command will do a manual fetch of mail channels. This will also "
"show errors that might appear within that process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:787
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channel.fetch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:791
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reprocess Failed Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:796
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"When Zammad fetches an email it cannot parse (e.g. due to a parser bug or a "
"malformed message), it will store the email in the database and warn in the "
"monitoring section about it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:800
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case of a malformed message (e.g. an invalid email address in one of the "
"header fields), you may need to manually edit the email before Zammad can "
"process it. To do so, follow the steps below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:801
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Export all Failed Emails to a Local Folder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:803
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:export_all`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:810
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can find the location of the exported email in the output of your "
"console.  Every time you perform an export of failed (unprocessable) emails, "
"it creates one folder containing all failed emails at the time of execution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:811
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Edit the Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:816
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The email has been exported in the step above. Now you can have a look at it "
"and try to repair it. Make sure to leave the file name untouched, as the "
"import will otherwise fail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:817
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import and Reprocess Locally Modified Email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:820
#, markdown-text
msgid "After editing the email, run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:821
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:import path/to/your/email.eml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:829
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This will apply your changes from the file to the database. You can also "
"pass the entire folder as argument, so all `.eml` files in it will we "
"imported and reprocessed. If the reprocessing of the email was successful, "
"the file(s) will be deleted, and the empty folder removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:830
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Make sure to run these commands only from the main Zammad folder\n"
"`/opt/zammad`. There may be problems if you try to run it from within\n"
"the generated subfolder.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:836
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Delete Unwanted Emails"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:840
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case of unwanted emails such as spam, you can delete them from the "
"database after exporting them with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:841
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:email_parser:failed_email:delete path/to/your/email.eml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:848
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you pass the export folder as argument instead, all contained emails will "
"be removed from the database, their files deleted and finally the empty "
"folder removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:849
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Show and Retry Failed Data Privacy Jobs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:853
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In rare cases, Zammad's data privacy jobs might fail. To show them, you can "
"use the following rake command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:854
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:data_privacy:failed:show\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:862
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To retry failed data privacy jobs, you can use the following "
"command. However, without changing the underlying issue that caused the "
"failure, the job will fail again. So make sure to check the logs for the "
"root cause of the failure and fix it before retrying the job."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:863
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:data_privacy:failed:retry\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:867
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fill a Test System With Test Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:869
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Don't run this in a productive environment! This can slow down Zammad\n"
"and is hard to revert!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:878
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The below command will add `50` agents, `1000` customers, `20` groups, `40` "
"organizations, `5` new overviews and `100` tickets. You can always use `0` "
"to not create specific items. Zammad will create random data which make no "
"logical sense."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:879
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"FillDb.load(agents: 50,customers: 1000,groups: 20,organizations: "
"40,overviews: 5,tickets: 100,)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:883
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deleting Records"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:885
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"☠️ The commands listed here cause **irrecoverable data loss**! Only\n"
"proceed if you know what you're doing and you\n"
"[have a backup](/en/tutorials/backup-restore)!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:891
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Removing Tickets (And Their Articles)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:894
#, markdown-text
msgid "Delete a ticket (specified by database ID):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:895
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.find(4).destroy\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:900
#, markdown-text
msgid "Delete all tickets:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:901
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:906
#, markdown-text
msgid "Keep some tickets (specified by database ID); delete the rest:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:907
#, no-wrap
msgid "tickets_to_keep = [1, 2, 3]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:911
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ticket.where.not(id: tickets_to_keep).destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:915
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Removing Users"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:917
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Customers **may not** be deleted while they have tickets remaining in\n"
"the system.\n"
"\n"
"As such, the examples below will delete not only the specified\n"
"customers, but **all tickets associated with them**, as well. Below\n"
"commands delete without any further warnings.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:926
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you're not sure what to do and need to learn more about what Zammad\n"
"does upon removing users, please consider using Zammad's UI options "
"instead.\n"
"You can find the data privacy feature in Zammad's admin interface under\n"
"_System > Data Privacy_.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:934
#, markdown-text
msgid "Removing users is possible in 2 ways: A single user and in bulk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:936
#, markdown-text
msgid "Remove a single user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:937
#, no-wrap
msgid "User.find_by(email: '<email address>').destroy\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:942
#, markdown-text
msgid "Remove several users:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:943
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"User.where(\n"
"      email: ['<email address 1>', '<email address 2>']\n"
"   ).destroy_all\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:949
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Removing Organizations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:951
#, no-wrap
msgid "Removing an organization does **not** delete associated customers.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:955
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Select organizations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:958
#, markdown-text
msgid "By \"active\" status:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:959
#, no-wrap
msgid "organizations = Organization.where(active: false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:964
#, markdown-text
msgid "By name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:965
#, no-wrap
msgid "organizations = Organization.where(name: 'Acme')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:970
#, markdown-text
msgid "By partial match on notes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:971
#, no-wrap
msgid "organizations = Organization.where('note LIKE ?', '%foo%')\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:975
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Preview affected organizations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:977
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"puts organizations.map { |org| \"ORGANIZATION #{org.name}\" "
"}.join(\"\\n\")\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:981
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Proceed with Deletion"
msgstr ""

