#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1028
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reset Zammad Installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (danger)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1030
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"Below commands are incomplete intentionally, error outputs will hint you\n"
"through! The following operations will cause data loss and are for\n"
"development / testing only.\n"
"\n"
"Don't forget to stop Zammad before trying to drop the database!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1040
#, markdown-text
msgid "Truncate the database:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1041
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:db:truncate\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1046
#, markdown-text
msgid "Migrate the database:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1047
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake db:migrate\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1052
#, markdown-text
msgid "Load the seed data:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1053
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake db:seed\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1058
#, markdown-text
msgid "Clear cache and reload the settings:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1059
#, no-wrap
msgid "rake zammad:db:rebuild\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rails-commands.md:1063
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"You can also use the `zammad:db:reset` command to reset your instance. This "
"task\n"
"will truncate the database, run the migrations, seed the database, clear "
"the\n"
"cache and reload the settings. However, it will not ask for your "
"confirmation\n"
"between each step, so you should use it with caution.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:1 src/en/reference/redis.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Redis Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad requires Redis to work. During package installation, it is installed "
"automatically unless there is a Redis installation on the host already. In "
"the Docker Compose stack, there is a Redis Service included. Both scenarios "
"work out of the box and should not require adjustments unless your setup "
"differs or you want to explicitly make adjustments."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:12
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Standard Setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For a Redis standard deployment, you can provide one variable: "
"`REDIS_URL`. This variable can include IP/URL, a port, a username and "
"password. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "`redis://redis.example.com:1234`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "`redis://user:password@redis.example.com`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sentinel Setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The variables in the table don't have default values set. In case you want "
"to connect Zammad to a Redis Sentinel cluster, only `REDIS_SENTINELS` "
"variable is mandatory, the others are optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/redis.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Variable                    | Description                                                                                                                                      "
"|\n"
"-----------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
" `REDIS_SENTINELS`           | Mandatory when using a Sentinel setup; comma "
"separated IPs/URLs; optional port. Examples: `sentinel1.example.com:26380`, "
"`sentinel2.example.com` |\n"
" `REDIS_SENTINEL_NAME`       | Name of Sentinel setup; fallback to "
"`mymaster` if not provided                                                                                   "
"|\n"
" `REDIS_SENTINEL_USERNAME`   | Username for Sentinel                                                                                                                            "
"|\n"
" `REDIS_SENTINEL_PASSWORD`   | Password for Sentinel                                                                                                                            "
"|\n"
" `REDIS_USERNAME`            | Username for Redis                                                                                                                               "
"|\n"
" `REDIS_PASSWORD`            | Password for Redis                                                                                                                               "
"|\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Some attributes of articles might not be straight forward or come with "
"fairly many options - below list hopefully helps you on this journey."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad supports `text/html` for HTML formatted text or `text/plain` for "
"plain text. This allows you to have better formatting options if you need "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Zammad web UI usually uses `text/html`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`type`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad supports a huge number of article types. Below list may be incomplete "
"depending on your instance and possibly installed add-ons / custom changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If not stated otherwise, all article types below are **communication "
"articles** and thus affecting SLA calculation in Zammad defaults."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The difference is that communication articles provide the option to reply "
"automatically. Which actions exactly are available depends on the article "
"type and e.g. recipient lists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`email`\n"
": This allows you to create incoming or outgoing email articles.\n"
"  However, this highly depends on the chosen `sender`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "`phone` : Indicates phone notes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:44
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`web`\n"
": Usually used by customers only. This type is being used when ever your\n"
"  customer uses the web UI to create articles.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:48
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`note`\n"
": When ever a communication does not fit (e.g.: internal notes) choose\n"
"  note. Zammad also uses this article type as default fall back.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  This is **not a communication article**.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:53
#, markdown-text
msgid "`sms` : This type is being used for Zammad's SMS integration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:57
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`chat`\n"
": This article type is technically a place holder and is only available\n"
"  via API.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:61
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`fax`\n"
": This article type is technically a place holder and is only available\n"
"  via API.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:66
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`twitter status` & `twitter direct-message`\n"
": These articles types are used by Zammad's twitter channel. Technically\n"
"  you can use these to automatically respond to existing requests via\n"
"  twitter.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:71
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`facebook feed post` & `facebook feed comment`\n"
": These articles types are used by Zammad's Facebook channel. Technically\n"
"  you can use these to automatically respond to existing requests via\n"
"  Facebook.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:75
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`telegram personal-message`\n"
": Used by Zammad's Telegram channel. Technically you can use these to\n"
"  automatically respond to existing requests via Telegram.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:81
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This attribute allows you to set the visibility of your articles. For "
"internal visible only use `true`, for visibly for your customers as well use "
"`false`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Visibility: internal doesn't mean it's silent**\n"
"\n"
"If you set an article to `internal: true` but choose to send an email,\n"
"please be aware that said email is still being sent out!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:89
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`sender`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:92
#, markdown-text
msgid "Indicates which use did create the article. You can choose from:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid "`Agent`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid "`Customer`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:96
#, markdown-text
msgid "`System`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/articles.md:97
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Depending of above selection, some article types may not be available\n"
"or behave different. Please be aware that `System` causes users not\n"
"being able to read the bodies (this works similar to Zammads trigger\n"
"displaying in tickets).\n"
msgstr ""

