#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:232
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Global Search"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:240
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you need to search not only in a specific object type, you can do so by "
"using the global search without specifying an object. The response may "
"include users, tickets, organizations, knowledge base articles and answers "
"and chats, depending on your system and content. This global search behaves "
"like the search in Zammad's UI in the left task bar. The available "
"parameters are different to the ones for the endpoint search."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:242
#, markdown-text
msgid "`GET`-Request sent: `/api/v1/search?query=welcome`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:243
#, no-wrap
msgid "<<< @/fixtures/rest-api/intro/get-global-search-res.json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:247
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Condition Based Search"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:253
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can even use conditions like for triggers and schedulers to search via "
"API. If you don't want to build such conditions manually, you can find a "
"hint below how to quickly build a condition structure via UI and fetch it "
"for your API request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:255
#, markdown-text
msgid "So, how do I build such a condition based request?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:265
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In Zammad, go to the admin interface and create a condition, e.g. by "
"creating a new overview or trigger. It can be inactive so you won't have any "
"unwanted actions or changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:265
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Go to the `Rails console </admin/console>`, either by using `rails c` / "
"`zammad run rails c` or adding the prefix `rails r` / `zammad run rails r` "
"in front of the commands below, depending on your setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:265
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Search for the created condition, adjust the following examples to your "
"needs:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:266
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"puts Overview.find_by(name: 'My test "
"overview').attributes.slice('condition').to_json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ruby)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:270
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"puts Trigger.find_by(name: 'My new test "
"trigger').attributes.slice('condition').to_json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:275
#, markdown-text
msgid "This leads to an output like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "<<< @/fixtures/rest-api/intro/condition-based-search.json\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:283
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Use this as payload in your `POST`-Request in an endpoint search. The "
"response includes the same objects as the trigger or overview you created."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:284
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sorting Search Results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:287
#, markdown-text
msgid "Zammad allows you to sort your search results by field if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:288
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`sort_by`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:292
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Append `?sort_by={row name}` to your query to sort by a specific row that "
"appears in the search result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:293
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`order_by`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:297
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Append `?order_by={direction}` to your query to switch in between ascending "
"and descending order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:299
#, markdown-text
msgid "Directions are: `asc` and `desc`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:300
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Usually you'll want to combine both parameters in your searches -\n"
"e.g.: `?query={search string}&sort_by={row name}&order_by={direction}`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:305
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Actions On Behalf of Other Users"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:309
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Requirement:** the user used for running the query on behalf requires\n"
"`admin.user` permission.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:312
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Running API queries on behalf of other users allows you to e.g. create "
"tickets by a different user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:315
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To do so, add a new HTTP header named `From` to your request. The value of "
"this header can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:319
#, markdown-text
msgid "user ID"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:319
#, markdown-text
msgid "user login"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:319
#, markdown-text
msgid "user email"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:321
#, markdown-text
msgid "`From` is available for all endpoints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:322
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:327
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The API expects UTF-8 encoding. Keep in mind that especially when using URLs "
"with get options (e.g. `?query=this`) you may need to encode your URL "
"accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:330
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you want to learn more about URL encoding, [this Wikipedia "
"article](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding) may be of help"
msgstr ""

#. type: Link reference
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:331
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[^1]: **Re**presentational **S**tate **T**ransfer - **A**pplication "
"**P**rogramming **I**nterface)"
msgstr ""

