#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Backup & Restore (Docker)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:9
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This section shows some basics about the backup and restore process for a "
"Docker Compose based deployment of Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you are familiar with volume based backup and restore procedures in "
"Docker, and perhaps already use a different method or tool, then you can "
"keep using it. A backup would typically mean shutting down the stack to "
"ensure all in-memory files get written to disk, then backing up the volume "
"contents, and then starting the stack again. When using such method, you can "
"consider using the [disable-backup-service "
"scenario](/en/reference/docker-compose-scenarios) so that the built-in "
"backup and restore mechanism of Zammad is not activated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The rest of this page describes the built-in backup and restore mechanism of "
"Zammad's Docker Compose stack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you're familiar with Docker, the sections below include the information "
"you'll need. The [Docker file handling](/en/tutorials/docker-file-handling) "
"page covers some examples about how to handle the backup files and to copy "
"it into a Docker volume to restore it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Backup"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"By default, a backup is created at each start of the stack as well as at 3 "
"o'clock each night. The backup is stored in the volume of the "
"**zammad-backup** container under `/var/tmp/zammad`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Restore"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Start the new stack at least once so a Zammad database is available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Stop the stack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you restore to a production stack with activated file system "
"storage, you should purge the content of the directory "
"`/opt/zammad/storage/` inside the volume. The restore process only "
"adds/overwrites files there, no cleanup will take place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Copy or move the backup files to `/var/tmp/zammad/restore/` inside the "
"volume of the **zammad-backup** container. Be aware that the restore process "
"always uses the latest backup according to the timestamp of the file "
"name. Only backups from package and Docker installations are supported by "
"this built-in backup method. Don't provide the `latest_zammad_*.gz` files "
"because they link to an unknown location for the restore process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Start the stack. The restore process is triggered if the `restore` directory "
"is detected and the backup files are in place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore-docker.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"After the restore process has finished, the `restore` directory got "
"renamed. You can safely delete it now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:1 src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Backup & Restore (Package)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:9
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Zammad ships scripts in package installations for backup & restore which you "
"can use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These scripts do not come with any warranty and may not work in your "
"specific\n"
"use case. This depends on the configuration and installation type of your\n"
"instance.\n"
"\n"
"You should always regularly test and review the functionality! If the "
"script\n"
"functionality or scope is not working for your cases, feel free to copy "
"these\n"
"to a independent location and adjust the scripts as needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "There are some limitations you should know:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "These scripts won't work in container based installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "They only work for PostgreSQL installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "The backup is always a full dump (no incremental backup)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Partial backup and restore (e.g. only specific data like tickets, users) is "
"not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Switching database system is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "System settings (like environment variables) are not backed up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Restore to an older Zammad version is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Do not restore backup files from custom scripts with the provided scripts by "
"Zammad. This might cause problems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The scripts are located in `/opt/zammad/contrib/backup`. The following files "
"are relevant:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Backup configuration file: `config.dist`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Script for backing up your data: `zammad_backup.sh`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "Script for restoring your data: `zammad_restore.sh`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"To execute a backup based on the default configuration, follow the steps "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Copy the `config.dist` file to `config`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Change default parameters in the config file if needed. See [Backup "
"Configuration](#backup-configuration) for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Stop Zammad `systemctl stop zammad`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Execute `/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_backup.sh` (as `root` or `zammad` "
"user)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Backup Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can find details about the configuration parameters with default values "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:60
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`BACKUP_DIR` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"/var/tmp/zammad_backup\"/>\n"
": Location where the script writes the backup files to. The directory will "
"be\n"
"  created if it does not exist. Make sure you have enough space because "
"the\n"
"  script writes full dumps.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:65
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`HOLD_DAYS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"10\"/>\n"
": Define how many days the backup script should keep old backups. This "
"value\n"
"  contains a 60 minutes grace period (e.g. 10 days plus 1 hour) for safety\n"
"  reasons. Old backups are removed before creating the a new backup.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Examples:\n"
"    - `1` will keep backups of the last 25 hours\n"
"    - `-1` will remove all available backups (except the new one)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`FULL_FS_DUMP` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"yes\"/>\n"
":   - `yes`: the backup includes also application files.\n"
"    - `no`: the backup includes only user data.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:76
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In any case, it includes the Zammad database and the attachments, if you\n"
"  stored them in the file system. If you are in doubt, set this to no.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:79
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`DEBUG` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"no\"/>\n"
": Setting this option to `yes` will output useful debug messages.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This option potentially returns sensitive information to standard output! "
"Do\n"
"  not use this option in production environments or ensure to turn it off "
"after\n"
"  testing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:85
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Restore Backups"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Important Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:90
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please read the following information carefully before starting to restore "
"your data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This section is **not** about **migrating from one host to another**. You "
"can find instructions about this topic on the [Migrate Zammad "
"page](migrate-host)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "This guide expects a fully installed Zammad version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "It also expects you to restore Zammad on the same host and Zammad version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The restore process stops & restarts Zammad. Therefore you have to run the "
"restore script with appropriate permissions (e.g. as root)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid "PostgreSQL based installations will drop and re-create the database!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:100
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"At least twice the backed up Zammad instance size of free storage is "
"required. If you have the dump only, factor 3 could be a good number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your scenario is different as described above, please consult the\n"
"[Zammad "
"Community](https://community.zammad.org/c/trouble-running-zammad-this-is-your-place/5){target=_blank}\n"
"or consider\n"
"[paid support "
"options](https://zammad.com/en/services/professional-services){target=_blank}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:108
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy Backup Files to a Fitting Location"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:112
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Ensure that the user you're using for restoration is allowed to read the "
"backup files and to write to `/opt/zammad/`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:114
#, markdown-text
msgid "The Zammad backup consists of two files. They are named like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (plain)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<timestamp>_zammad_db.psql.gz\n"
"<timestamp>_zammad_files.tar.gz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:122
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"There are also two symlinks in your backup directory pointing to the newest "
"backup created:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (plain)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"latest_zammad_db.psql.gz\n"
"latest_zammad_files.tar.gz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:130
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Copy them to a fitting location which is accessible for the user who "
"executes the restore script."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:131
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configure Backup Script"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:135
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"For a new installation, this is required. At least you have to provide a "
"directory where your backups are stored. See [Backup "
"Configuration](#backup-configuration) for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:136
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clean Up the Storage Folder"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:141
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In case you restore to a production environment with activated filesystem "
"storage, you should purge the content of the directory "
"`/opt/zammad/storage/` inside the volume. The restore process only "
"adds/overwrites files there, no cleanup will take place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:142
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the Restore"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:148
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Be aware that restoring backups can overwrite your `database.yml`. You can\n"
"check that by looking into the `[...]_zammad_files.tar.gz` file. If there\n"
"is a `database.yml` in the directory _config > database_, ensure to save "
"the\n"
"original version **before restoring**.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:151
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The restore works in two possible ways, depending on how interactive you "
"want to go:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:152
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Interactive restore (recommended)\n"
"Run the script:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_restore.sh\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Provide the requested information to the script and wait for the restore\n"
"process to finish. Depending on the size of your backup and host "
"performance,\n"
"this may take some time.\n"
"\n"
"=== Non-interactive restore\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs|warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:152
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only use the following option if you know what you're doing! The following\n"
"command will overwrite existing data without further prompts!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:152
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When called with a timestamp argument (matching the backups filename),\n"
"Zammad will proceed immediately to restoring the specified backup.\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_restore.sh 20170507121848\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:181
#, markdown-text
msgid "The result should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ansi)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:182
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Zammad restore started - Fri Jan 21 17:54:13 CET 2022!\n"
"\n"
"The restore will delete your current database!\n"
"Be sure to have a backup available!\n"
"\n"
"Please ensure to have twice the storage of the uncompressed backup size!\n"
"\n"
"Note that the restoration USUALLY requires root permissions as services are "
"stopped!\n"
"\n"
"Enter 'yes' if you want to proceed!\n"
"Restore?: yes\n"
"Enter file date to restore:\n"
"20220120124714\n"
"20220121175344\n"
"File date: 20220121175344\n"
"Enter db date to restore:\n"
"20220120124714\n"
"20220121175344\n"
"DB date: 20220121175344\n"
"# Stopping Zammad\n"
"# Checking requirements\n"
"# ... Dropping current database zammad\n"
"Dropped database 'zammad'\n"
"# ... Creating database zammad for owner zammad\n"
"CREATE DATABASE\n"
"# Restoring PostgreSQL DB\n"
"# Restoring Files\n"
"# Ensuring correct file permissions ...\n"
"# Clearing Cache ...\n"
"# Starting Zammad\n"
"\n"
"# Zammad restored successfully - Fri Jan 21 17:54:34 CET 2022!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:225
#, markdown-text
msgid "If you've set any environmental settings, please re-apply them now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:225
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If not already done, [install "
"Elasticsearch](/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch) now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:225
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"[Connect Elasticsearch with Zammad and rebuild its search "
"index](/en/tutorials/connect-config-elasticsearch). The rebuild can safely "
"run during your work, but will cause a degraded search performance and may "
"lead to temporarily not found data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:226
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting Backup & Restore"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:232
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You can find some common problems below. If your issue is not listed, feel "
"free to consult the [Zammad "
"Community](https://community.zammad.org/c/trouble-running-zammad-this-is-your-place/5){target=_blank} "
"for technical assistance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:233
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Exit Codes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:237
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Our backup & restore scripts come with exit codes to help you finding a "
"solution. However, we do not guarantee a complete error handling."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:240
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Beside the exit codes, there are also error messages returned to standard "
"out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:247
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code | Description / Situation                                                                                                                                                                "
"|\n"
"|------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| `0`  | The script finished successfully (or the error is not handled).                                                                                                                        "
"|\n"
"| `1`  | This is a general error. Most often used for script aborts due to "
"incorrect information provided or information missing.                                                               "
"|\n"
"| `2`  | There was an error with database handling. This usually either "
"happens if your database server does not meet script requirements, login "
"data being invalid or \"broken‟ database dumps. |\n"
"| `3`  | There were issues with file / folder permissions.                                                                                                                                      "
"|\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:248
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Common Problems"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:250
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Password Authentication Failed / Peer Authentication Failed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:255
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This indicates that the password of your Zammad DB user is either different "
"from your `database.yml` or the wrong database server may be contacted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:258
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your Zammad instance is running, it can be caused by falling back to "
"socket connection which is why you didn't notice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:260
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:271
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**What to do?**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:264
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Ensure that the provided user credentials are correct. You can also consider "
"to use the `reset_db_password` script, you can find in the backup directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:265
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ident Authentication Failed for User"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:269
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This indicates your database server does require `ident` authentication.  "
"That authentication method is not supported by our scripts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:274
#, markdown-text
msgid "Check the `pg_hba.conf` of your PostgreSQL-Server and adjust it if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:276
#, markdown-text
msgid "Usually, authentication can be allowed like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:277
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# THIS IS A SAMPLE AND MAY NOT FIT YOUR ENVIRONMENT\n"
"host    all             all             127.0.0.1/32            md5\n"
"host    all             all             ::1/128                 md5\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:286
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Please consult the official [PostgreSQL "
"documentation](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/){target=_blank} for this, as "
"this is out of our documentation scope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ####
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:287
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "WARNING: You don't Seem to Have Any Attachments in the File System"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:291
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This indicate that your instance currently does not save attachments to file "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:294
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This warning will be shown once before creating an empty directory to allow "
"the backup process to continue successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:298
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
