#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install Elasticsearch 9"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide shows a simple standard installation of Elasticsearch 9. The "
"intention is to get you up and running quickly.  However, in case you need a "
"more advanced configuration or face any issues, have a look at the [official "
"Elasticsearch installation "
"documentation](https://www.elastic.co/docs/deploy-manage/deploy/self-managed/installing-elasticsearch){target=_blank}.  "
"Adapt it wherever needed in case your use-case differs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Repository Key"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs key:distros)
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Ubuntu/Debian\n"
"\n"
"Install required tools:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo apt install curl apt-transport-https\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Add repo key:\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"curl -fsSL https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch | \\\n"
"  gpg --dearmor | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/elasticsearch-keyring.gpg "
"\\\n"
"  && sudo chmod 644 /usr/share/keyrings/elasticsearch-keyring.gpg\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== OpenSUSE/SLES\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"sudo rpm --import https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS/RHEL\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"sudo rpm --import https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Add Repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs key:distros)
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:53
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Ubuntu/Debian\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"echo \"deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/elasticsearch-keyring.gpg] "
"https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/9.x/apt stable main\" | sudo tee "
"/etc/apt/sources.list.d/elastic-9.x.list\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== OpenSUSE/SLES\n"
"\n"
"Create the file `/etc/zypp/repos.d/elasticsearch.repo` and add:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"[elasticsearch]\n"
"name=Elasticsearch repository for 9.x packages\n"
"baseurl=https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/9.x/yum\n"
"gpgcheck=1\n"
"gpgkey=https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"enabled=0\n"
"autorefresh=1\n"
"type=rpm-md\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS/RHEL\n"
"\n"
"Create the file `/etc/yum.repos.d/elasticsearch.repo` and add:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"[elasticsearch]\n"
"name=Elasticsearch repository for 9.x packages\n"
"baseurl=https://artifacts.elastic.co/packages/9.x/yum\n"
"gpgcheck=1\n"
"gpgkey=https://artifacts.elastic.co/GPG-KEY-elasticsearch\n"
"enabled=0\n"
"type=rpm-md\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs key:distros)
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Ubuntu/Debian\n"
"\n"
"``` sh\n"
"sudo apt update && sudo apt install elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== OpenSUSE/SLES\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo zypper modifyrepo --enable elasticsearch && sudo zypper install "
"elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS/RHEL\n"
"\n"
"RHEL 7 or earlier:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo yum install --enablerepo=elasticsearch elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"CentOS and RHEL 8 and later:\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo dnf install --enablerepo=elasticsearch elasticsearch\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Make sure to check the output and to copy the password of the built-in "
"superuser. Otherwise, you have to recreate it by\n"
"running `/usr/share/elasticsearch/bin/elasticsearch-reset-password -u "
"elastic`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:129
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/install-elasticsearch.md:133
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Optionally, check and configure Elasticsearch’s configuration file which you "
