#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reporting with Grafana"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:8
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide is about Grafana. If you want to use another tool, check if it\n"
"supports Elasticsearch indexes. If yes, then you are good to go!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Grafana is a third party analytics/visualization application you can connect "
"to Zammad (precisely: Elasticsearch). It can access the Elasticsearch index "
"and visualize your Zammad data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide will provide you some steps to get started. For a deeper insight "
"you should consider having a look at [Elasticsearch's indexed "
"attributes](/en/reference/es-indexed-attributes) and to read the "
"[documentation of Grafana](https://grafana.com/docs/){target=_blank}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide expects all requirements to be up and running. We will not cover "
"core configurations of each tool. Please also note that we can't support you "
"with configuration of your specific third party tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "You need:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"A running instance of Grafana (hosted or self-hosted) in version 10.3 or "
"higher"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "Read access to your Elasticsearch index"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "A Zammad instance in version 4 or higher"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/reporting-grafana.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Never expose Elasticsearch to the public if you're not sure how\n"
"to do it. Especially **never** without authentication! Zammad\n"
"stores **very sensitive** information within the Elasticsearch\n"
"Index.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
