#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single Sign-on with Kerberos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Single Sign-On for Kerberos <Badge type=\"warning\" text=\"on-premise "
"only\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This guide will discuss how to set up single sign-on using Microsoft Active "
"Directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conceptual Overview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Like every other web application out there, Zammad has its own logic for "
"signing users up, storing their passwords, authenticating them, and managing "
"their sessions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If your IT department keeps its own user identity store (like Active "
"Directory), Zammad's SSO support allows you to leverage that existing auth "
"system so that anyone with an account on your local intranet will 1) "
"automatically have an account in Zammad and 2) be able to log in with a "
"single click."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you don't have this IT infrastructure but still want one-click\n"
"login, you can use alternatives like Github, Google, Facebook and more.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:28
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "How Does it Work?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Once enabled, single sign-on activates an endpoint at "
"`https://your.zammad.host/auth/sso`. When the Zammad server receives a GET "
"request at this endpoint with a valid username in **any one of the "
"following** entities, it creates a new session for that user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "an `X-Forwarded-User` request header"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "a `REMOTE_USER` web server environment variable"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "an `HTTP_REMOTE_USER` web server environment variable"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Wait. SSO allows you to sign in with only a username?**\n"
"\n"
"In principle, yes.\n"
"\n"
"**How is that okay?**\n"
"\n"
"In this guide, we configure our web server (Apache) to intercept all\n"
"requests to the `/auth/sso` endpoint. Instead of forwarding them to\n"
"Zammad, Apache initiates a three-sided login process (_Kerberos\n"
"authentication_) between the itself, the user, and the Active\n"
"Directory server.\n"
"\n"
"If Active Directory doesn't recognize the user or their password,\n"
"Zammad never sees the request, and the session is never created.\n"
"\n"
"**What does this all mean?**\n"
"\n"
"It means there are many ways you could set up SSO—you don't need to\n"
"follow this guide or even use Active Directory or Kerberos—but if you\n"
"don't know what you're doing, you're going to end up with a _massive_\n"
"security hole.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Too busy to handle it on your own?**\n"
"\n"
"We've got you covered. Our experts offer custom-tailored workshops to\n"
"get your team up and running fast and with confidence.\n"
"[Just drop us a line](https://zammad.com/contact){target=_blank}!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:74
#, markdown-text
msgid "You will need:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "a Microsoft Active Directory environment with"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "root access"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "support for AES 256-bit encryption"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "a Zammad host with"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "a fully-qualified domain name (FQDN)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:82
#, markdown-text
msgid "some familiarity with system administration (e.g. Apache configuration)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:87
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For best results, set up the LDAP integration to make sure\n"
"your Active Directory and Zammad user accounts are always in sync. You\n"
"can find it in Zammad's admin interface under\n"
"_Settings > Security > Third-party Applications_.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:88
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Configure Active Directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:94
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In the Kerberos authentication scheme, the **authentication server** (Active "
"Directory) needs to maintain shared secrets with the **service** "
"(Zammad). To make this possible, we need to register a **service principal "
"name** (SPN) for Zammad on Active Directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "These directions have been confirmed on Windows Server 2016.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:99
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1a. Create a service account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:103
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"You may use an existing service account if you have one. Admin privileges "
"are not required; a normal user account will do."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:105
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"![Screenshot Active Directory service account "
"settings](/screenshots/sso-kerberos/active-directory-service-account-settings.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:106
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1b. Reset Password"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:110
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Reset service account password after enabling the \"This account supports "
"Kerberos AES 256 bit encryption\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:111
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1c. Register a SPN for Zammad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:114 src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:351
#, markdown-text
msgid "Replace the following placeholders in the commands below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:121 src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:356
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:438
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<zammad-host>`: Zammad FQDN"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:121
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<service-acct>`: Service account logon name"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:121
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<password>`: Password of the service account (Option `/pass *` did prove to "
"not work)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:121 src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:311
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:356 src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:438
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<domain>`: Windows domain"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:121
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<master-domain-controller>`: Master domain controller IP/FQD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:123
#, markdown-text
msgid "The commands below will prompt for the users password:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "setspn -s HTTP/<zammad-host> <service-acct>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:128
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ktpass /princ HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN> \\\n"
"        /mapuser <service-acct> \\\n"
"        /crypto AES256-SHA1 \\\n"
"        /ptype KRB5_NT_PRINCIPAL \\\n"
"        /pass <password> -SetPass +DumpSalt \\\n"
"        /target <master-domain-controller> \\\n"
"        /out zammad.keytab\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:138
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1d. Note the secret key and version number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:142
#, markdown-text
msgid "The output of the command above contains important data for Step 2e below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:143
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using legacy password setting method\n"
"Failed to set property 'servicePrincipalName' to 'HTTP/<zammad-host>' on Dn "
"'CN=Zammad Service,DC=<domain>,DC=<tld>': 0x13.\n"
"WARNING: Unable to set SPN mapping data.\n"
"If <service-acct> already has an SPN mapping installed for "
"HTTP/<zammad-host>, this is no cause for concern.\n"
"Building salt with principalname HTTP/<zammad-host> and domain <domain> "
"(encryption type 18)...\n"
"Hashing password with salt \"<domain><service-acct>\".\n"
"Key created.\n"
"Output keytab to zammad.keytab:\n"
"Keytab version: 0x502\n"
"keysize 67 <service-acct>@<domain> ptype 1 (KRB5_NT_PRINCIPAL) vno 3 etype "
"0x12 (AES256-SHA1) keylength 32 "
"(0x5ee827c30c736dd4095c9cbe146eabc216415b1ddb134db6aabd61be8fdf7fb1) # "
"[!code focus]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:157
#, markdown-text
msgid "On the last line, take note of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:160
#, markdown-text
msgid "the secret key in parentheses at the end (**0x5ee827...**)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:160
#, markdown-text
msgid "the secret key version number preceded by `vno` (**3**)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:161
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Remove NGINX, Set up Apache + Kerberos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:165
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Next, the Zammad host must be configured to support Kerberos (and to accept "
"auth credentials provided by the Active Directory server)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:169
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"In most cases, you would have to recompile NGINX from source with an extra "
"module to enable Kerberos support. To get around this, we will use Apache, "
"which offers Kerberos support through a plug-in module instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "All commands in this section must be run as root (or with `sudo`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:174
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2a. Turn Off NGINX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:176
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This will take your Zammad instance **offline** until Apache is fully\n"
"configured and running.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:182
#, markdown-text
msgid "Turn off Nginx:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:183
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo systemctl stop nginx\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:188
#, markdown-text
msgid "Keep it off after reboot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo systemctl disable nginx\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:196
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you wish to minimize downtime, you can save this step for last; just bear "
"in mind that Apache will not start if the port it wants to listen on is "
"being used by NGINX."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:199
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"If you can't complete this tutorial for any reason, simply turn off Apache "
"and restore NGINX:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (details)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:200
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl stop apache2\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl disable apache2\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl enable nginx\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl start nginx\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:220
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2b. Pre-Configure Apache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:226
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"This documentation expects an already working Apache configuration.  You "
"should have a look at the [webserver configuration "
"guide](/en/tutorials/webserver-config) before continuing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:227
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2c. Install Further Apache Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:229
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian & Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo apt update\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo apt install krb5-user libapache2-mod-auth-gssapi\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo yum install krb5-workstation mod_auth_kerb\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo zypper ref\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo zypper install krb5-client apache2-mod_auth_kerb\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:259
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2d. Enable Apache Modules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:263
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"SSO requires modules that are not enabled by default. By default you can use "
"`a2enmod` to do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:264
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== a2enmod (Debian & Ubuntu)\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"a2enmod auth_gssapi rewrite\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl restart apache2\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== a2enmod (OpenSUSE)\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"a2enmod auth_kerb rewrite\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo systemctl restart apache2\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== via configuration file (CentOS)\n"
"\n"
"add/uncomment the appropriate `LoadModule` statements in your Apache\n"
"config:\n"
"\n"
"```apache\n"
"# /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf\n"
"\n"
"LoadModule auth_kerb_module /usr/lib/apache2/modules/mod_auth_kerb.so\n"
"LoadModule rewrite_module modules/mod_rewrite.so\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:300
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2e. Configure Kerberos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:304
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Kerberos realm configuration is how you tell the Zammad server how to reach "
"the _domain controller_ (Active Directory server)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:306
#, markdown-text
msgid "Replace the following placeholders in the sample config below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:311
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<domain-controller>`: Domain controller IP/FQDN(s)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:311
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"`<master-domain-controller>`: Master domain controller IP/FQDN (must not be "
"read-only, but can be the same as `<domain-controller>`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (ini)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:312
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# /etc/krb5.conf\n"
"\n"
"[libdefaults]\n"
"   default_realm = <DOMAIN>\n"
"\n"
"   default_tkt_enctypes = aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96\n"
"   default_tgs_enctypes = aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96\n"
"   permitted_enctypes = aes256-cts-hmac-sha1-96\n"
"\n"
"   kdc_timesync = 1\n"
"   ccache_type = 4\n"
"   forwardable = false\n"
"   proxiable = false\n"
"   fcc-mit-ticketflags = false\n"
"\n"
"[realms]\n"
"         # multiple KDCs ok (one `kdc = ...` definition per line)\n"
"         <DOMAIN> = {\n"
"                  kdc = <domain-controller>\n"
"                  admin_server = <master-domain-controller>\n"
"                  default_domain = <domain>\n"
"\n"
"                  # below is only for GSSAPI\n"
"                  auth_to_local = "
"RULE:[1:$1@$0](.*@<domain>)s/@<domain>$//\n"
"                  auth_to_local = DEFAULT\n"
"         }\n"
"\n"
"[domain_realm]\n"
"         .<domain> = <DOMAIN>\n"
"         <domain> = <DOMAIN>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:345
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2f. Generate Keytab"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:349
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Apache needs a Kerberos _keytab_ (key table) to manage its shared secrets "
"with the domain controller."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:356
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<secret-key>`: Secret key (**omit the leading** `0x`)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:356
#, markdown-text
msgid "`<vno>`: Secret key version number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:359
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"The secret key and version number were found in `sso-register-spn` (Step 1d)  "
"above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:361
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter ktutil:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:362
#, no-wrap
msgid "ktutil\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:367
#, markdown-text
msgid "Add keytab:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:368
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ktutil: addent -key -p HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN> -k <vno> -e aes256-cts\n"
"Key for HTTP/<zammad-host>@<domain> (hex): <secret-key>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:374
#, markdown-text
msgid "Confirm the entry was added successfully:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:375
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ktutil: list\n"
"slot KVNO Principal\n"
"---- ---- ---------------------------------------------------------------\n"
"   1    3 HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:383
#, markdown-text
msgid "Write keytab to disk:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:384
#, no-wrap
msgid "ktutil: wkt /root/zammad.keytab\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:389
#, markdown-text
msgid "Leave ktutil:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:390
#, no-wrap
msgid "ktutil: quit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:396
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Then, place the keytab in the Apache config directory and set the "
"appropriate permissions:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:397
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian, Ubuntu, OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo mv /root/zammad.keytab /etc/apache2/\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo chown root:www-data /etc/apache2/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo chmod 640 /etc/apache2/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo mv /root/zammad.keytab /etc/httpd/\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo chown root:apache /etc/httpd/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"sudo chmod 640 /etc/httpd/zammad.keytab\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:429
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2g. Configure Apache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:433
#, markdown-text
msgid ""
"Add the following directive to the end of the virtual host configuration "
"file to create your Kerberos SSO endpoint at `/auth/sso`:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:435
#, markdown-text
msgid "Replace the following placeholders in the command below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:439
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Debian & Ubuntu\n"
"\n"
"``` apache\n"
"# /etc/apache2/sites-available/zammad.conf\n"
"\n"
"<LocationMatch \"/auth/sso\">\n"
"   SSLRequireSSL\n"
"   AuthType GSSAPI\n"
"   AuthName \"Your Zammad\"\n"
"   GssapiBasicAuth On\n"
"   GssapiCredStore keytab:/etc/apache2/zammad.keytab\n"
"   GssapiLocalName On\n"
"   require valid-user\n"
"\n"
"   RewriteEngine On\n"
"   RewriteCond %{LA-U:REMOTE_USER} (.+)\n"
"   RewriteRule . - [E=RU:%1,NS]\n"
"   RequestHeader set X-Forwarded-User \"%{RU}e\" env=RU\n"
"</LocationMatch>\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"=== CentOS & OpenSUSE\n"
"\n"
"The configuration for CentOS and OpenSUSE below contains two\n"
"`Krb5KeyTab` lines! Keep only the one you need.\n"
"\n"
"``` apache\n"
"# /etc/apache2/sites-available/zammad.conf\n"
"\n"
"<LocationMatch \"/auth/sso\">\n"
"   SSLRequireSSL\n"
"   AuthType Kerberos\n"
"   AuthName \"Your Zammad\"\n"
"   KrbMethodNegotiate On\n"
"   KrbVerifyKDC On\n"
"   KrbMethodK5Passwd On\n"
"   KrbAuthRealms <DOMAIN>\n"
"   KrbLocalUserMapping on                 # strips @REALM suffix from "
"REMOTE_USER variable\n"
"   KrbServiceName HTTP/<zammad-host>@<DOMAIN>\n"
"   Krb5KeyTab /etc/apache2/zammad.keytab  # Ubuntu, Debian, & openSUSE\n"
"   Krb5KeyTab /etc/httpd/zammad.keytab    # CentOS\n"
"   require valid-user\n"
"\n"
"   RewriteEngine On\n"
"   RewriteCond %{LA-U:REMOTE_USER} (.+)\n"
"   RewriteRule . - [E=RU:%1,NS]\n"
"   RequestHeader set X-Forwarded-User \"%{RU}e\" env=RU\n"
"</LocationMatch>\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:493
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2g. Restart Apache to Apply Changes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/tutorials/sso-kerberos.md:495
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:176
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo systemctl restart apache2\n"
msgstr ""

